    (104, NULL, 'The Grand Inquisitor', '{}', '2026-01-16 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-16 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Grand Inquisitor, by Fyodor Dostoevsky.', NULL, 'Russian', '2010-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL29306488W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (105, NULL, 'Uncle''s Dream and the Permanent Husband', '{}', '2026-01-16 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-16 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Uncle''s Dream and the Permanent Husband, by Fyodor Dostoevsky.', NULL, 'Russian', '2013-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14252142-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10989309-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL22163471W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (106, NULL, 'War and Peace', '{}', '2026-01-16 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-16 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'War and Peace delineates in graphic detail events surrounding the French invasion of Russia, and the impact of the Napoleonic era on Tsarist society, as seen through the eyes of five Russian aristocratic families.\nThe novel begins in the year 1805 during the reign of Tsar Alexander I and leads up to the 1812 French invasion of Russia by Napoleon. The era of Catherine the Great (1762 – 1796), when the royal court in Paris was the centre of western European civilization, is still fresh in the minds of older people. Catherine, fluent in French and wishing to reshape Russia into a great European nation, made French the language of her royal court. For the next one hundred years, it became a social requirement for members of the Russian nobility to speak French and understand French culture. This historical and cultural context in the aristocracy is reflected in War and Peace. Catherine\'s grandson, Alexander I, came to the throne in 1801 at the age of 24.', NULL, 'Russian', '1845-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12621906-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8236285-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL267171W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_and_Peace}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (107, NULL, 'Voskresenīe', '{}', '2026-01-16 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-16 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Resurrection , the last full-length novel written by Leo Tolstoy, was published in 1899 after ten years in the making. A humanitarian cause — the pacifist Doukhobor sect, persecuted by the Russian government, needed funds to emigrate to Canada — prompted Tolstoy to finish the novel and dedicate its ensuing revenues to alleviate their plight. Ultimately, Tolstoy’s actions were credited with helping hundreds of Doukhobors emigrate to Canada. \n The novel centers on the relationship between Nekhlúdoff, a Russian landlord, and Máslova, a prostitute whose life took a turn for the worse after Nekhlúdoff wronged her ten years prior to the novel’s events. After Nekhlúdoff happens to sit in the jury for a trial in which Máslova is accused of poisoning a merchant, Nekhlúdoff begins to understand the harm he has inflicted upon Máslova — and the harm that the Russian state and society inflicts upon the poor and marginalized — as he embarks on a quest to alleviate Máslova’s suffering.', NULL, 'Russian', '1899-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6309101-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10529049-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL457760W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resurrection_(Tolstoy_novel)}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (108, NULL, 'Khozi͡ain i rabotnik', '{}', '2026-01-16 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-16 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"Master and Man" (Russian: Хозяин и работник) is an 1895 short story by Leo Tolstoy.', NULL, 'Russian', '1895-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9907988-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11150525-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15236124W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (109, NULL, 'Tolstoy', '{}', '2026-01-16 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-16 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Tolstoy, by Leo Tolstoy.', NULL, 'Russian', '1994-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/613116-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL267127W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (110, NULL, 'Boyhood', '{}', '2026-01-16 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-16 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Boyhood, by Leo Tolstoy.', NULL, 'Russian', '1854-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4986307-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7432952-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL267182W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boyhood_(novel)}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (111, NULL, 'The Kreutzer sonata and other stories', '{}', '2026-01-17 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'"In "What For?" a Polish family suffers in the aftermath of the insurrection of 1830 to 1831, and in its suffering Tolstoy expresses his outrage at a Russian autocracy whose disastrous policies in the nineteenth century sowed the seeds of revolt in the twentieth. "Divine and Human" takes place around the time of the assassination of the emperor Alexander II in 1881.\n\nA revolutionary terrorist, pondering the Gospels in his jail cell, is converted to a Tolstoyan understanding of true life, while an old schismatic\'s faith in himself is destroyed by an encounter in prison. In "Berries," Tolstoy condemns the frivolity of the 1905 revolution by contrasting the ridiculous conversations of liberals with the innocent labor of peasant children."--BOOK JACKET.', NULL, 'Russian', '1887-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11725468-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8215237-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15088382W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (112, NULL, 'Youth', '{}', '2026-01-17 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Youth, by Leo Tolstoy.', NULL, 'Russian', '1986-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2762013-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7206966-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL25375900W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Youth_(Tolstoy_novel)}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (113, NULL, 'Hadji-Mourad', '{}', '2026-01-17 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'In this short novel, Tolstoy fictionalizes the final days of Hadji Murád, a legendary Avar separatist who fought against, and later with, Russia, as the Russian Empire was struggling to annex Chechnya and the surrounding land in the late 1840s. \n The novel opens with the narrator finding a thistle crushed in a blooming field, which reminds him of Hadji Murád and his tragic tale. As the narrator recounts the story, the reader is quickly thrust into the rich, colorful history of the Caucuses, and its people’s fight against Russian imperialism. \n Hadji Murád is portrayed as a legendary and imposing, yet friendly and approachable figure. Despite his reputation, it seems that his best days are behind him; as the novel opens, Murád is fleeing Shamil, a powerful imam who has captured Murád’s family. Murád finds himself thrust between the invading Russians on one side, and Shamil’s vengeance on the other. \n As Murád and his tiny but loyal group of warriors try to forge alliances in their attempt to rescue Murád’s family, they quickly find themselves politically outclassed.', NULL, 'Russian', '1900-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/605982-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13317186-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL457431W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (114, NULL, 'Father Sergius', '{}', '2026-01-17 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Vers l''annee 1840, St-Petersbourg fut bouleverse par un evenement dont tous resterent stupefaits: le beau prince Kassatski, chef de l''escadron d''elite du regiment des cuirassiers, futur aide de camp de l''empereur Nicolas 1er, etait alors fiance a une haute dame de la cour, non seulement celebre pour sa beaute, mais encore en grande faveur aupres de l''Imperatrice. Soudain, un mois avant le mariage, Kassatski auquel on pouvait predire la plus brillante carriere aupres de Nicolas Ier, brisa ses fiancailles, donna sa demission et ayant legue son bien a sa sur, partit pour un monastere avec la volonte de se faire moine.', NULL, 'Russian', '1998-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1760955-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11262200-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL267175W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (115, NULL, 'Vlastʹ tʹmy', '{}', '2026-01-17 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Power of Darkness is a five-act drama that follows the downfall of the peasants Anísya and Nikíta as they succumb to a series of sordid temptations, from adultery and drunkenness to outright murder. Written in 1886 but suppressed by censors until 1902, the play is a realist portrayal of some of the darkest elements of Russian peasant life. Similar to some other late Tolstoy works, like Resurrection , the play’s psychological exploration of human depravity is accompanied by a sharp social critique of the Russian Empire and its role in perpetuating poverty and ignorance among its lowest and most marginalized classes.', NULL, 'Russian', '1887-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5442204-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1281099-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL457787W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Power_of_Darkness}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (116, NULL, 'Pride and Prejudice', '{}', '2026-01-17 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Pride and Prejudice is an 1813 novel of manners written by Jane Austen. The novel follows the character development of Elizabeth Bennet, the dynamic protagonist of the book who learns about the repercussions of hasty judgments and comes to appreciate the difference between superficial goodness and actual goodness.\n\nMr. Bennet, owner of the Longbourn estate in Hertfordshire, has five daughters, but his property is entailed and can only be passed to a male heir. His wife also lacks an inheritance, so his family faces becoming very poor upon his death. Thus, it is imperative that at least one of the girls marry well to support the others, which is a motivation that drives the plot.', NULL, 'English', '1813-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14348537-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8748572-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66554W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pride_and_Prejudice}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (117, NULL, 'Emma', '{}', '2026-01-17 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Emma, by Jane Austen, is a novel about youthful hubris and the perils of misconstrued romance. The novel was first published in December 1815. As in her other novels, Austen explores the concerns and difficulties of genteel women living in Georgian-Regency England; she also creates a lively comedy of manners among her characters. Before she began the novel, Austen wrote, "I am going to take a heroine whom no one but myself will much like." In the very first sentence she introduces the title character as "Emma Woodhouse, handsome, clever, and rich." Emma, however, is also rather spoiled, headstrong, and self-satisfied; she greatly overestimates her own matchmaking abilities; she is blind to the dangers of meddling in other people''s lives; and her imagination and perceptions often lead her astray.', NULL, 'English', '1815-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9278312-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13748222-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66513W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (118, NULL, 'Sense and Sensibility', '{}', '2026-01-17 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When Mr. Dashwood dies, he must leave the bulk of his estate to the son by his first marriage, which leaves his second wife and three daughters (Elinor, Marianne, and Margaret) in straitened circumstances. They are taken in by a kindly cousin, but their lack of fortune affects the marriageability of both practical Elinor and romantic Marianne. When Elinor forms an attachment for the wealthy Edward Ferrars, his family disapproves and separates them. And though Mrs. Jennings tries to match the worthy (and rich) Colonel Brandon to her, Marianne finds the dashing and fiery Willoughby more to her taste. Both relationships are sorely tried. But this is a romance, and through the hardships and heartbreak, true love and a happy ending will find their way for both the sister who is all sense and the one who is all sensibility. - Publisher.', NULL, 'English', '1811-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9278292-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9064719-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66562W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (119, NULL, 'Persuasion', '{}', '2026-01-17 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Persuasion tells the love story of Anne Elliot and Captain Frederick Wentworth, whose sister rents Miss Elliot''s father''s house, after the Napoleonic Wars come to an end. The story is set in 1814. The book itself is Jane Austen''s last published book, published posthumously in December of 1818.', NULL, 'English', '1789-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12824691-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9278303-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66544W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (120, NULL, 'Mansfield Park', '{}', '2026-01-17 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-17 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Fanny Price is born to a poor family, but is sent to her mother''s rich relations to be brought up with her cousins. There she is treated as an inferior by all except her cousin Edmund, whose kindness towards her earns him her steadfast love. Fanny is quiet and obedient and does not come into her own until her elder cousins leave the estate following a scandalous play put on in their father''s absence. Fanny''s loyalty and love is tested by the beautiful Crawford siblings. But their essentially weak natures and morals show them for what they really are, and allow Fanny to gain the one thing she truly desires.', NULL, 'English', '1814-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14618737-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66530W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (121, NULL, 'Northanger Abbey', '{}', '2026-01-18 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Northanger Abbey is both a perfectly aimed literary parody and a withering satire of the commercial aspects of marriage among the English gentry at the turn of the nineteenth century. But most of all, it is the story of the initiation into life of its naïve but sweetly appealing heroine, Catherine Morland, a willing victim of the contemporary craze for Gothic literature who is determined to see herself as the heroine of a dark and thrilling romance.\n\nWhen Catherine is invited to Northanger Abbey, the grand though forbidding ancestral seat of her suitor, Henry Tilney, she finds herself embroiled in a real drama of misapprehension, mistreatment, and mortification, until common sense and humor — and a crucial clarification of Catherine’s financial status — puts all to right. Written in 1798 but not published until after Austen’s death in 1817, Northanger Abbey is characteristically clearheaded and strong, and infinitely subtle in its comedy.', NULL, 'English', '1818-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12567961-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12333984-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66534W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (122, NULL, 'Lady Susan', '{}', '2026-01-18 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Beautiful, flirtatious, and recently widowed, Lady Susan Vernon seeks an advantageous second marriage for herself, while attempting to push her daughter into a dismal match. A magnificently crafted novel of Regency manners and mores that will delight Austen enthusiasts with its wit and elegant expression', NULL, 'English', '1925-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12641526-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13458152-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66614W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (123, NULL, 'Love and Freindship', '{}', '2026-01-18 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Love and Friendship is presented in the form of letters exchanged between the heroine, Laura, and the daughter of her friend Isabel, Marianne. In an effort to guide Marianne through the pitfalls of life, Laura relates her own hilarious misadventures — from her quick marriage to the rebellious son of a baronet to an exciting journey to Scotland with her best friend.', NULL, 'English', '1995-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12641527-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12025907-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15079937W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (124, NULL, 'Sanditon', '{}', '2026-01-18 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Charlotte Heywood, a young woman from the country, encounters a sophisticated, if cynical, world in the rapidly developing resort town of Sanditon.', NULL, 'English', '1975-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14620845-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4724993-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66575W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (125, NULL, 'The Watsons', '{}', '2026-01-18 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Watsons, by Jane Austen.', NULL, 'English', '1923-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9279171-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11679220-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66613W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (126, NULL, 'Frankenstein; or, The Modern Prometheus', '{}', '2026-01-18 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Frankenstein; or, The Modern Prometheus is an 1818 novel written by English author Mary Shelley. Frankenstein tells the story of Victor Frankenstein, a young scientist who creates a sapient creature in an unorthodox scientific experiment. Shelley started writing the story when she was 18, and the first edition was published anonymously in London on 1 January 1818, when she was 20. Her name first appeared in the second edition, which was published in Paris in 1821.', NULL, 'English', '1818-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12356249-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10872750-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL450063W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankenstein}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (127, NULL, 'The Last Man', '{}', '2026-01-18 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Mary Shelley, the author of [Frankenstein], wrote the apocalyptic novel The Last Man in 1826. Its first person narrative tells the story of our world standing at the end of the twenty-first century and - after the devastating effects of a plague - at the end of humanity. In the book Shelley writes of weaving this story from a discovery of prophetic writings uncovered in a cave near Naples. The Last Man was made into a 2008 film.', NULL, 'English', '1826-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/882662-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/574771-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL450124W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (128, NULL, 'Mathilda', '{}', '2026-01-18 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Relatando la historia desde su lecho de muerte, Matilda cuenta la historia de la confesión de su padre sobre el amor incestuoso que sentía hacia ella, seguido por su suicidio mediante ahogamiento; su relación con un talentoso poeta joven llamado Woodville fracasa ante el objetivo de remendar las emociones de Matilda o prevenir su muerte solitaria.', NULL, 'English', '1959-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1759946-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1720670-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL450120W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (129, NULL, 'The Mortal Immortal', '{}', '2026-01-18 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Mortal Immortal, by Mary Shelley.', NULL, 'English', '1996-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13171944-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15380992W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (130, NULL, 'Frankenstein', '{}', '2026-01-18 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-18 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Frankenstein, by Mary Shelley.', NULL, 'English', '1987-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13114822-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL33035718W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (131, NULL, 'Falkner', '{}', '2026-01-19 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Mary Shelley, the celebrated author of Frankenstein, scrutinizes the developing impact of Indian culture on a young English soldier, Falkner. As a child Falkner was mistreated and neglected at home and at school. While in the company of Mrs. Rivers and her daughter, Alithea, he is inspired to end grievous habits. But his schooldays are brought to a sudden end when he cuts the head of an usher with a knife in an abusive struggle. His uncle then places him in the East Indian military college. While there, Falkner learns of Mrs. Rivers'' death, discovers that he loves Alithea, and asks her father''s permission to marry her. Her father refuses so Falkner sails to India as an officer of the East India company''s cavalry, still believing that Alithea will someday be his bride. Stationed in India, Falkner witnesses the subjugation of the overwhelmed natives. He learns their language and traditions but also tries to Westernize them with more enlightened social ethics. These divergent attitudes are a reflection of his developing cultural indecisiveness.', NULL, 'English', '1837-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1979512-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8863726-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL449979W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (132, NULL, 'Proserpine & Midas', '{}', '2026-01-19 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Proserpine & Midas, by Mary Shelley.', NULL, 'English', '1922-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2784641-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12089643-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL450122W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (133, NULL, 'Lodore', '{}', '2026-01-19 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'A London visit unfolds like a quiet storm, testing loyalties, love, and a family’s secrets.\n\nTwo women, an unsettled marriage, and a man with a shadowed past drive a tale of social intrigue and fragile bonds. From the drawing rooms of the capital to an unexpected journey, this edition follows the characters as they navigate memory, duty, and a world that reshapes their fates.\n\nThe narrative centers on Ethel and her guardianship by relatives in a bustling city that challenges their sense of belonging. With wit and sharp observation, the text explores how public life and private loyalties collide, and how a single encounter can alter the course of many lives.', NULL, 'English', '1835-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/770179-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1800488-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL450056W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (134, NULL, 'Mary Shelley''s Frankenstein; or, the Modern Prometheus (1818 text)', '{}', '2026-01-19 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'This is the original edition which was published in 3 volumes. The cover photograph is of Volume 1.\nPublished anonymously. By Mary Wollstonecraft Shelley.\nFirst edition.\nWith half-titles.\nTitle page with quote from Milton\'s Paradise Lost: "Did I request thee, maker, from my clay / To mould me man? Did I solicit thee / From darkness to promote me?"\nPrinter statement from title page verso of volume 1; place of printing follows printer.\nPagination: volume 1: xii, 181, pages; volume 2: , 156 pages; volume 3: , 192, pages.\nPublisher\'s advertisements on 2 unnumbered pages at end of volume 1 and 2 unnumbered pages at the end of volume 3.', NULL, 'English', '1818-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7267770-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL25595002W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (135, NULL, 'The Fortunes Of Perkin Warbeck A Romance', '{}', '2026-01-19 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Fortunes Of Perkin Warbeck A Romance, by Mary Shelley.', NULL, 'English', '1830-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1802492-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5811603-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL449981W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (136, NULL, 'Dracula', '{}', '2026-01-19 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Na história, um casal e seus amigos são atormentados por Conde Drácula, uma entidade sobrenatural e hematófoga que, presa em uma maldição contagiosa, pretende se mudar de seu recluso castelo na Transilvânia para a efervescente Londres do século XIX. Com a ajuda do professor Van Helsing, o grupo de amigos pretende enfrentar o morto-vivo, mesmo com todos os perigos que a ofensiva trará.', NULL, 'English', '1897-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12216503-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/106193-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85892W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (137, NULL, 'Dracula''s Guest and Other Weird Stories', '{}', '2026-01-19 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Dracula’s Guest (1914) is a collection of short stories by Irish author Bram Stoker. Edited and published by Florence, the author’s wife, following Stoker’s death only two years prior, Dracula’s Guest helped to establish the Irish master of Gothic horror’s reputation as a leading writer of the early-twentieth century.', NULL, 'English', '1937-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2039484-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8912252-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85889W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (138, NULL, 'The Jewel of Seven Stars', '{}', '2026-01-19 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'This dark fantasy Bram Stoker book is full of suspense. Set in ancient Egypt, it will keep you on the edge of your seat with a twist Please Note: This book is easy to read in true text, not scanned images that can sometimes be difficult to decipher. This eBook has bookmarks at chapter headings and is printable up to two full copies per year.at the end. A must for Bram Stoker fans.', NULL, 'English', '1902-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2760301-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9064734-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85891W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (139, NULL, 'The lair of the white worm', '{}', '2026-01-19 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The lair of the white worm, by Bram Stoker.', NULL, 'English', '1911-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2039486-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85890W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (140, NULL, 'The Lady of the Shroud', '{}', '2026-01-19 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-19 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Lady of the Shroud, by Bram Stoker.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2998388-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85888W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (141, NULL, 'The Man', '{}', '2026-01-20 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Man, by Bram Stoker.', NULL, 'English', '1905-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2998389-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9182657-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85887W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (142, NULL, 'Personal Reminiscences Of Henry Irving V1', '{}', '2026-01-20 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Personal Reminiscences Of Henry Irving V1, by Bram Stoker.', NULL, 'English', '1906-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2493160-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5741133-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85872W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (143, NULL, 'Famous impostors', '{}', '2026-01-20 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Famous impostors, by Bram Stoker.', NULL, 'English', '1910-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4807497-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10261539-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85884W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (144, NULL, 'Under the Sunset', '{}', '2026-01-20 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A short story collection featuring nine tales of the macabre.', NULL, 'English', '1882-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1472654-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85885W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (145, NULL, 'The mystery of the sea', '{}', '2026-01-20 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The mystery of the sea, by Bram Stoker.', NULL, 'English', '1902-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/494178-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9186645-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85883W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (146, NULL, 'The Murders in the Rue Morgue', '{}', '2026-01-20 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"The Murders in the Rue Morgue" is a short story by Edgar Allan Poe published in Graham''s Magazine in 1841. It has been described as the first modern detective story; Poe referred to it as one of his "tales of ratiocination". C. Auguste Dupin is a man in Paris who solves the mystery of the brutal murder of two women.', NULL, 'English', '1841-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11774455-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6791850-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL41072W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (147, NULL, 'The Narrative of Arthur Gordon Pym', '{}', '2026-01-20 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'From the book:UPON my return to the United States a few months ago, after the extraordinary series of adventure in the South Seas and elsewhere, of which an account is given in the following pages, accident threw me into the society of several gentlemen in Richmond, Va., who felt deep interest in all matters relating to the regions I had visited, and who were constantly urging it upon me, as a duty, to give my narrative to the public. I had several reasons, however, for declining to do so, some of which were of a nature altogether private, and concern no person but myself, others not so much so. One consideration which deterred me was, that, having kept no journal during a greater portion of the time in which I was absent, I feared I should not be able to write, from mere memory, a statement so minute and connected as to have the appearance of that truth it would really possess, barring only the natural and unavoidable exaggeration to which all of us are prone when detailing events which have had powerful influence in exciting the imaginative faculties.', NULL, 'English', '1838-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7160877-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/103064-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL40962W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Narrative_of_Arthur_Gordon_Pym_of_Nantucket}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (148, NULL, 'The Raven', '{}', '2026-01-20 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"The Raven" is a narrative poem by American writer Edgar Allan Poe. First published in January 1845, the poem is often noted for its musicality, stylized language, and supernatural atmosphere. It tells of a talking raven''s mysterious visit to a distraught lover, tracing the man''s slow descent into madness. The poem makes use of folk, mythological, religious, and classical references. "The Raven" was first attributed to Poe in print in the New York Evening Mirror on January 29, 1845.', NULL, 'English', '1845-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8246077-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/785950-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL41081W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Raven}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (149, NULL, 'The Fall of the House of Usher', '{}', '2026-01-20 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"The Fall of the House of Usher" is a short story by American writer Edgar Allan Poe, first published in 1839 in Burton''s Gentleman''s Magazine, then included in the collection Tales of the Grotesque and Arabesque in 1840. The short story, a work of Gothic fiction, includes themes of madness, family, isolation, and metaphysical identities.', NULL, 'English', '1704-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11838138-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11382841-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL41078W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fall_of_the_House_of_Usher}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (150, NULL, 'The Gold-Bug', '{}', '2026-01-20 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-20 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The discovery of a message in code on a shoreline formerly infested with pirates sends William Legrand and his friends on a hunt for buried treasure.', NULL, 'English', '1845-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11777143-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4975466-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL40983W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (151, NULL, 'Eureka', '{}', '2026-01-21 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"This edition puts Eureka in context, explaining Poe''s excellent grasp of then-new developments in astronomy, his often-prescient considerations of what was known and what might come next. (Poe is especially good on space-time) and the close connections between Eureka and the thought and attitudes of his era." "Through extensive annotations this edition of Eureka demonstrates intimate connections with Poe''s poetry, fiction, and criticism; with his career and aspirations, his humor and satire; and with his love of grand literary effects."--BOOK JACKET.', NULL, 'English', '1848-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11752466-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/146822-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL41076W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (152, NULL, 'The Black Cat', '{}', '2026-01-21 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'"The Black Cat" is a short story by American writer Edgar Allan Poe. It was first published in the August 19, 1843, edition of The Saturday Evening Post. In the story, an unnamed narrator has a strong affection for pets until he perversely turns to abusing them.\n\n----------\nThis story also contained in:\n18 Best Stories\n6 nouvelles fantastiques\nBest Horror Stories\nBest Known Works of Edgar Allan Poe\nBest Short Stories\nBest Short Stories of Edgar Allan Poe\nCampfire Chillers\nCharles Keeping\'s Book of Classic Ghost Stories\nChat noir et autres contes fantastiques\nChat noir et autres nouvelles\nChat noir et autres nouvelles\nChat noir et autres nouvelles\nChat noir et autres récits fantastique\nClosed on Account of Rabies\nComplete Poems of Edgar Allan Poe Together with a selection from his stories\nComplete Stories and Poems of Edgar Allan Poe\nComplete Tales & Poems of Edgar Allan Poe\nComplete Tales and Poems\nComplete Tales and Poems of Edgar Allan Poe\nCreepy Classics II\nCuentos clásicos del norte: Primera Serie\nEdgar Allan Poe Reader\nEdgar Allan Poe\'s Tales of Mystery and Madness\nEssential', NULL, 'English', '1968-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11709016-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6967311-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL41068W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Black_Cat_(short_story)}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (153, NULL, 'The Purloined Letter', '{}', '2026-01-21 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"The Purloined Letter" is a short story by American author Edgar Allan Poe. It is the third of his three detective stories featuring the fictional C. Auguste Dupin, the other two being "The Murders in the Rue Morgue" and "The Mystery of Marie Rogêt". These stories are considered to be important early forerunners of the modern detective story. It first appeared in the literary annual The Gift for 1845 (1844) and soon was reprinted in numerous journals and newspapers.', NULL, 'English', '1931-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11674884-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6952550-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL41065W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Purloined_Letter}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (154, NULL, 'The Pit and the Pendulum', '{}', '2026-01-21 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"The Pit and the Pendulum" is a short story by American writer Edgar Allan Poe and first published in 1842 in the literary annual The Gift: A Christmas and New Year''s Present for 1843. The story is about the torments endured by a prisoner of the Spanish Inquisition, though Poe skews historical facts. The narrator of the story describes his experience of being tortured. The story is especially effective at inspiring fear in the reader because of its heavy focus on the senses, such as sound, emphasizing its reality, unlike many of Poe''s stories which are aided by the supernatural. The traditional elements established in popular horror tales at the time are followed, but critical reception has been mixed. The tale has been adapted to film several times.', NULL, 'English', '1962-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11872237-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/916060-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL273550W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pit_and_the_Pendulum}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (155, NULL, 'The Masque of the Red Death', '{}', '2026-01-21 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'"The Masque of the Red Death" (originally published as "The Mask of the Red Death: A Fantasy") is a short story by American writer Edgar Allan Poe, first published in 1842. The story follows Prince Prospero\'s attempts to avoid a dangerous plague, known as the Red Death, by hiding in his abbey. He, along with many other wealthy nobles, hosts a masquerade ball in seven rooms of the abbey, each decorated with a different color. In the midst of their revelry, a mysterious figure disguised as a Red Death victim enters and makes his way through each of the rooms. Prospero dies after confronting this stranger, whose "costume" proves to contain nothing tangible inside it; the guests also die in turn.\n\nThe story was first published in May 1842 in Graham\'s Magazine and has since been adapted in many different forms, including a 1964 film starring Vincent Price. Poe\'s short story has also been alluded to by other works in many types of media.', NULL, 'English', '1982-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11860130-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8348135-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL41050W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Masque_of_the_Red_Death}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (156, NULL, 'The Call of the Wild', '{}', '2026-01-21 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'As Buck, a mixed breed dog, is taken away from his home, instead of facing a feast for breakfast and the comforts of home, he faces the hardships of being a sled dog. Soon he lands in the wrong hands, being forced to keep going when it is too rough for him and the other dogs in his pack. He also fights the urges to run free with his ancestors, the wolves who live around where he is pulling the sled.', NULL, 'English', '1903-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12393037-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8236400-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14942956W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Call_of_the_Wild}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (157, NULL, 'The Iron Heel', '{}', '2026-01-21 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Generally considered to be "the earliest of the modern Dystopian," it chronicles the rise of an oligarchic tyranny in the United States. It is arguably the novel in which Jack London''s socialist views are most explicitly on display. A forerunner of soft science fiction novels and stories of the 1960s and 1970s, the book stresses future changes in society and politics while paying much less attention to technological changes.', NULL, 'English', '1907-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243314-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9926811-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL74502W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (158, NULL, 'Burning Daylight', '{}', '2026-01-21 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Burning Daylight was Jack London''s best selling book during his lifetime. The book begins as a two-fisted macho adventure on the Klondike, as the hero--nicknamed Burning Daylight--becomes the most successful entrepreneur during the Alaskan Gold Rush. After acheiving his fame and fortune, he finds no more challenge in the north and heads to the States for new worlds to conquer. He is flim-flammed out of his fortune by Wall Streeters, learns the lesson of dog-eat-dog, and becomes as much of a scoundrel as those who robbed him.', NULL, 'English', '1910-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8245391-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11111692-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL144821W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_Daylight}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (159, NULL, 'White Fang', '{}', '2026-01-21 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The story of a wolf/dog cross, who is raised by Indians, and becomes a deadly fighter.', NULL, 'English', '1905-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8236920-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8893058-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL74504W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Fang}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (160, NULL, 'Children of the Frost', '{}', '2026-01-21 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-21 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Children of the Frost, by Jack London.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9383224-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11354923-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL144813W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (161, NULL, 'The Sea-Wolf', '{}', '2026-01-22 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Jack London''s novel The Sea Wolf became an instant bestseller on its release in 1904. Ambrose Bierce wrote "The great thing - and it is among the greatest of things - is that tremendous creation, Wolf Larsen...the hewing out and setting up of such a figure is black for a man to do in one lifetime." The Sea Wolf tells the story of intellectual Humphrey van Weyden''s toughening and growth in the face of brutality and hardship. Set adrift after his ferry collides in fog and sinks, van Weyden is pulled out of the sea by Wolf Larsen.', NULL, 'English', '1900-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8236975-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10606923-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL144824W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sea-Wolf}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (162, NULL, 'Before Adam', '{}', '2026-01-22 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A young man in modern America is terrorized by visions of an earlier, primitive life. Across the enormous chasm of thousands of centuries, his consciousness has become entwined with that of Big-Tooth, an ancestor living at the dawn of humanity. Big-Tooth makes his home in Pleistocene Africa, a ferocious, fascinating younger world torn by incessant conflict between early humans and protohumans. Before Adam is a remarkable and provocative tale that thrust evolution further into the public spotlight in the early twentieth century and has since become a milestone of speculative fiction. The brilliance of the book lies not only in its telling but also in its imaginative projection of a mindset for early humans. Capitalizing on his recognized ability to understand animals, Jack London paints an arresting and dark portrait of how our distant ancestors thought about themselves and their world.', NULL, 'English', '1906-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243967-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10306789-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL74501W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (163, NULL, 'Martin Eden', '{}', '2026-01-22 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Jack London\'s Martin Eden was first published in 1909 and is the story of a young writer\'s quest for celebrity and love. Much loved by writers who identify with Martin\'s belief that when he posted a manuscript, \'there was no human editor at the other end, but a mere cunning arrangement of cogs that changed the manuscript from one envelope to another and stuck on the stamps,\' that automatically returned it slapped with a rejection slip.\n\n---\n\nAlso contained in:\n\n- Best of Jack London\n- The Collected Jack London\n- Novels and Social Writings', NULL, 'English', '1908-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9223765-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8277235-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL144822W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Eden}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (164, NULL, 'John Barleycorn', '{}', '2026-01-22 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'It all came to me one election day. It was on a warm California afternoon, and I had ridden down into the Valley of the Moon from the ranch to the little village to vote Yes and No to a host of proposed amendments to the Constitution of the State of California. Because of the warmth of the day I had had several drinks before casting my ballot, and divers drinks after casting it. Then I had ridden up through the vine-clad hills and rolling pastures of the ranch, and arrived at the farm-house in time for another drink and supper.', NULL, 'English', '1913-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11954493-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12010780-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL144798W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Barleycorn_(novel)}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (165, NULL, 'Smoke Bellew', '{}', '2026-01-22 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Smoke Bellew, by Jack London.', NULL, 'English', '1912-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9383283-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11290295-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15031788W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaska-Kid}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (166, NULL, 'Treasure Island', '{}', '2026-01-22 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Traditionally considered a coming-of-age story, Treasure Island is an adventure tale known for its atmosphere, characters and action, and also as a wry commentary on the ambiguity of morality — as seen in Long John Silver — unusual for children''s literature then and now. It is one of the most frequently dramatized of all novels. The influence of Treasure Island on popular perceptions of pirates is enormous, including treasure maps marked with an "X", schooners, the Black Spot, tropical islands, and one-legged seamen carrying parrots on their shoulders', NULL, 'English', '1880-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13859660-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8229197-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24034W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (167, NULL, 'The Strange Case of Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde', '{}', '2026-01-22 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Mr. Gabriel Utterson is a serious, austere lawyer living a humdrum life in Victorian London. Yet there is a strange clause in his friend, Dr. Henry Jekyll\'s will: should he disappear for more than 3 months, everything will be inherited by Hyde. But after Edward Hyde\'s darker nature is revealed one dark winters night, Mr. Utterson begins to investigate the connection between the two men, and finds the dark secret binding them closer then he could have ever thought imaginable.\n\nAdapted countless times in film, some times in video game form, and referenced countless times in popular culture, here is the story that started it all: The Strange Case of Dr. Jekyll & Mr. Hyde!', NULL, 'English', '1875-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/295773-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7887036-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24156W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (168, NULL, 'Kidnapped', '{}', '2026-01-22 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'KIDNAPPED is an adventure story that has become the model for any thriller of escape and suspense. \n\nSet in 1751, the flight of David Balfour and Alan Breck across the Highlands of Scotland is based on real events. Though he wrote the book to make money, while living as an invalid in Bournemouth. Stevenson was proud of it; he inscribed a presentation copy with the couplet. Here is the one sound page of all my writing. The one I\'m proud of and that I delight in. Rowland Hilder is famous for his paintings of the English countryside but his work in book illustration covered a much wider canvas. His drawing for KIDNAPPED were first published in 1930 and have undeservedly, been long out of print.\n\nA sixteen-year-old orphan is kidnapped by his villainous uncle, but later escapes and becomes involved in the struggle of the Scottish highlanders against English rule.', NULL, 'English', '1886-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8267822-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5268612-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24166W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (169, NULL, 'The  black arrow', '{}', '2026-01-22 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Richard Shelton is a young knight during the Wars of the Roses. We see him ascend and rescue his lady love. He then seeks revenge against his father''s murderer, but when the evidence points towards his guardian he is forced to go into hiding. He joins the band of outlaws known as the Black Arrow.', NULL, 'English', '1888-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8239493-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1279046-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24161W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (170, NULL, 'David Balfour', '{}', '2026-01-22 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-22 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'From the book:It is the fate of sequels to disappoint those who have waited for them; and my David, having been left to kick his heels for more than a lustre in the British Linen Company’s office, must expect his late re-appearance to be greeted with hoots, if not with missiles. Yet, when I remember the days of our explo-rations, I am not without hope. There should be left in our native city some seed of the elect; some long-egged, hot-headed youth must repeat to-day our dreams and wanderings of so many years ago; he will relish the pleasure, which should have been ours, to follow among named streets and numbered houses the country walks of David Balfour, to identify Dean, and Silvermills, and Broughton, and Hope Park, and Pilrig, and poor old Lochend - if it still be standing, and the Figgate Whins - if there be any of them left; or to push (on a long holiday) so far afield as Gillane or the Bass. So, perhaps, his eye shall be opened to behold the series of the generations, and he shall weigh with surprise his momentous and nugatory gift of life.', NULL, 'English', '1883-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8244483-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12133050-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24163W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (171, NULL, 'The master of Ballantrae', '{}', '2026-01-23 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Master of Ballantrae: A Winter''s Tale is one of Stevenson''s darker, more political novels. Two brothers are brought into conflict by the Jacobite rising of 1745, which tears their family apart.', NULL, 'English', '1888-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8230370-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5996459-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24164W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (172, NULL, 'New Arabian Nights', '{}', '2026-01-23 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'During his residence in London, the accomplished Prince Florizel of Bohemia gained the affection of all classes by the seduction of his manner and by a well-considered generosity. He was a remarkable man even by what was known of him; and that was but a small part of what he actually did. Although of a placid temper in ordinary circumstances, and accustomed to take the world with as much philosophy as any ploughman, the Prince of Bohemia was not without a taste for ways of life more adventurous and eccentric than that to which he was destined by his birth.', NULL, 'English', '1882-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9243741-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8244571-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24158W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (173, NULL, 'Travels with a donkey in the Cevennes', '{}', '2026-01-23 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Travels with a Donkey in the Cevennes recounts Robert Louis Stevenson''s 120 mile, 12 day hike, accompanied only by his stubborn and unwieldy donkey, through the Cevennes of south-central France. A pioneering piece of outdoor literature, it is one of Stevenson''s earliest works, and one of the earliest accounts of hiking and camping for recreation rather than necessity. Stevenson''s route is still popular today; recently when asked why the Scotsman still informs the identity of the Cevennes, a politician and historian of the area remarked "Because he showed us the landscape that makes us who we are."', NULL, 'English', '1879-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8245405-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24153W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (174, NULL, 'An Inland voyage', '{}', '2026-01-23 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Robert Louis Stevenson''s 1878 travelogue, An Inland Voyage, details his canoeing trip through France and Belgium in 1876. Pioneering new ground in outdoor literature, this was Stevenson''s first book. He had decided to become free from his parent''s financial support so that he might freely pursue the woman he loved; to support himself he wrote travelogues, most notably An Inland Voyage, Travels with a Donkey in the Cevennes and The Silverado Squatters. Stevenson undertook the journey with his friend, Sir Walter Grindlay Simpson, at a time when such outdoor travel for leisure was considered unusual and it resulted in this romantic and original work that still inspires travelers today.', NULL, 'English', '1878-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8245458-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15923277W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (175, NULL, 'Poems', '{}', '2026-01-23 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'An illustrated collection of thirty-two popular poems by Robert Louis Stevenson, mostly from "A Child''s Garden of Verses." Includes an introduction about the poet''s life and work.', NULL, 'English', '1896-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8244441-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15403167W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (176, NULL, 'The Secret Garden', '{}', '2026-01-23 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A ten-year-old orphan comes to live in a lonely house on the Yorkshire moors where she discovers an invalid cousin and the mysteries of a locked garden.', NULL, 'English', '1911-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12622062-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9025496-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69612W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (177, NULL, 'Little Lord Fauntleroy', '{}', '2026-01-23 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Cedric himself knew nothing whatever about it. It had never been even mentioned to him. He knew that his papa had been an Englishman, because his mamma had told him so; but then his papa had died when he was so little a boy that he could not remember very much about him, except that he was big, and had blue eyes and a long mustache, and that it was a splendid thing to be carried around the room on his shoulder.\n\n----------\n###German-language description:\nDer siebenjährige Cedric lebt mit seiner verwitweten Mutter in New York in ärmlichen Verhältnissen, als sich das Leben des Jungen schlagartig ändert: Er soll ein Lord werden! Sein Großvater, der mürrische Graf von Dorincourt, möchte seinen einzigen Enkel zu sich nach England holen und dort zu seinem standesgemäßen Erben erziehen lassen. So macht sich die kleine Familie auf den Weg in die Alte Welt.', NULL, 'English', '1886-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/29376-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/105848-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69625W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (178, NULL, 'A Little Princess', '{}', '2026-01-23 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'This is a story about a different kind of princess than one might imagine; a princess that is an orphan - lonely, cold, hungry and abused. Sara Crewe begins life as the beloved, pampered daughter of a rich man. When he dies a pauper, she is thrown on the non-existent mercy of her small-minded, mercenary boarding school mistress. Stripped of all her belongings but for one set of clothes and a doll, Sara becomes a servant of the household. Hated by the schoolmistress for her independent spirit, Sara becomes a pariah in the household, with only a few secretly loyal friends. But through her inner integrity and strength of will, Sara Crewe maintains the deportment, inner nobility and generous spirit of a "real" princess.', NULL, 'English', '1905-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2328315-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2804853-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69630W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (179, NULL, 'The Making of a Marchioness and The Methods of Lady Waldenhurst', '{}', '2026-01-23 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Making of a Marchioness and The Methods of Lady Waldenhurst, by Frances Hodgson Burnett.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/540027-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1716218-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69635W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (180, NULL, 'The Lost Prince', '{}', '2026-01-23 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-23 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Marco Loristan, exiled with his father from war-torn Samavia, meets a London street urchin who leads him into political intrigue.', NULL, 'English', '1915-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6462803-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5696176-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69633W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (181, NULL, 'The Land of the Blue Flower', '{}', '2026-01-24 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Hoping to dispel dark thoughts and evil from his corrupt kingdom, young King Amor proclaims an unconventional law and watches for the expected transformation.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5702352-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11062195-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69693W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (182, NULL, 'A Lady of Quality', '{}', '2026-01-24 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A Lady of Quality, by Frances Hodgson Burnett.', NULL, 'English', '1896-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/756376-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8999915-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69699W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (183, NULL, 'A Fair Barbarian', '{}', '2026-01-24 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'From the book:Slowbridge had been shaken to its foundations. It may as well be explained, however, at the outset, that it would not take much of a sensation to give Slowbridge a great shock. In the first place, Slowbridge was not used to sensations, and was used to going on the even and respectable tenor of its way, regarding the outside world with private distrust, if not with open disfavor. The new mills had been a trial to Slowbridge, - a sore trial. On being told of the owners'' plan of building them, old Lady Theobald, who was the corner-stone of the social edifice of Slowbridge, was said, by a spectator, to have turned deathly pale with rage; and, on the first day of their being opened in working order, she had taken to her bed, and remained shut up in her darkened room for a week, refusing to see anybody, and even going so far as to send a scathing message to the curate of St. James, who called in fear and trembling, because he was afraid to stay away. "With mills and mill-hands," her ladyship announced to Mr.', NULL, 'English', '1881-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2753868-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2808303-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69700W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (184, NULL, 'The Head of the House of Coombe', '{}', '2026-01-24 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Head of the House of Coombe, by Frances Hodgson Burnett.', NULL, 'English', '1922-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5570343-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8264837-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69695W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (185, NULL, 'The making of a marchioness', '{}', '2026-01-24 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'First published in 1901, The Making of a Marchioness follows thirty-something Emily who lives alone, humbly and happily, in a tiny apartment and on a meager income. She is the one that everyone counts on but no one goes out of their way to accommodate. This Cinderella-like story remains a much-loved favorite among many.\n\nThis book is followed by a sequel, The Methods of Lady Walderhurst. Later, the two novels were combined into Emily Fox-Seton.', NULL, 'English', '1901-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5652006-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7967383-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL69685W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (186, NULL, 'Little Women', '{}', '2026-01-24 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Louisa May Alcotts classic novel, set during the Civil War, has always captivated even the most reluctant readers. Little girls, especially, love following the adventures of the four March sisters--Meg, Beth, Amy, and most of all, the tomboy Jo--as they experience the joys and disappointments, tragedies and triumphs, of growing up. This simpler version captures all the charm and warmth of the original.', NULL, 'English', '1848-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8775559-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6795866-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL29983W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (187, NULL, 'Jo''s Boys', '{}', '2026-01-24 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'This sequel to Alcott''s "Little Women" and "Little Men" chronicles the return of the classmates of Plumfield, Jo''s school for boys. Readers reencounter Nat, the orphaned street musician, now a conservatory student; restless Dan, back from the gold mines of California; business-minded Tom; and other old friends.', NULL, 'English', '1886-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13166184-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2379041-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL26668762W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (188, NULL, 'Eight cousins', '{}', '2026-01-24 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Rose, a shy orphan, blossoms in the company of her spirited relatives when she takes up residence at "The Aunt Hill." This captivating novel by the author of Little Women offers readers of all ages endearing, inspiring stories about growing up, making friends, and facing life with kindness and courage.', NULL, 'English', '1874-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8143360-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6622592-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17846238W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (189, NULL, 'Little men', '{}', '2026-01-24 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'The characters from Little Women grow up and begin new adventures at Plumfield, a progressive school founded by Jo and her husband, Professor Bhaer.\n\nFollows the adventures of Jo March and her husband Professor Bhaer as they try to make their school for boys a happy, comfortable, and stimulating place.--LibraryThing\n\nWith two sons of her own, and twelve rescued orphan boys filling the informal school at Plumfield, Jo March -- now Jo Bhaer -- couldn\'t be happier. But despite the warm and affectionate help of the whole March family, boys have a habit of getting into scrapes, and there are plenty of troubles and adventures in store.--goodreads', NULL, 'English', '1885-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8043576-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/313266-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17761452W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (190, NULL, 'An Old-Fashioned Girl', '{}', '2026-01-24 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-24 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Polly visits her wealthy friend Fanny Shaw in the city and is overwhelmed by the fashionable and urban life they live--but also left out because of her "countrified" manners and outdated clothes.', NULL, 'English', '1869-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8244533-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2963076-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL29970W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (191, NULL, 'Rose in Bloom', '{}', '2026-01-25 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'In this sequel to Eight Cousins, Rose Campbell returns to the "Aunt Hill" after two years of traveling around the world. Suddenly, she is surrounded by male admirers, all expecting her to marry them. But before she marries anyone, Rose is determined to establish herself as an independent young woman. Besides, she suspects that some of her friends like her more for her money than for herself.', NULL, 'English', '1876-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7242794-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8248426-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL30020W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (192, NULL, 'Under the Lilacs', '{}', '2026-01-25 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Ben and his trained dog, Sancho, run away from the circus and soon find a warm welcome in a kind community where spirited games are played. Theatricals and imaginative pageantry are all part of the fun.', NULL, 'English', '1878-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7386602-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8249972-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL30065W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (193, NULL, 'Jack and Jill', '{}', '2026-01-25 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When friends Jack and Jill are injured in a sledding accident, their family and friends rally around them to help in their recovery.', NULL, 'English', '1880-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5922002-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8229277-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL30033W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (194, NULL, 'A Garland for Girls', '{}', '2026-01-25 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'This is a series of vignettes by Louisa May Alcott that illustrate the idea by Sir Philip Sidney that "They are never alone that are accompanied with noble thoughts." The reader is introduced to several young women who discover great satisfaction when they do what each can do and still have a renewed desire to be of more assistance while also witnessing the more somber parts of life. In "Pansies" Mrs. Warburton assures others that "hearts don''t break if they know where to go for strength." Ruth asks in "Water-lilies" if she can be forgiven her modesty, courage, and faithfulness. Rosamund of "Little Button Rose" declares "you''ve made my troubles go, can''t I make yours?" Finally in "Mountain-Laurel" Becky realizes that she can become a more useful and honored woman by putting the directives of her poetry into her life than by singing for her fame. For the characters of Alcott''s Garland, "When everything seemed darkest, good luck came." Please Note: This book has been reformatted to be easy to read in true text, not scanned images that can sometimes be difficult to decipher.', NULL, 'English', '1887-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9177025-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9205279-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15188919W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (195, NULL, 'Good wives', '{}', '2026-01-25 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Three years from Little Women, this is the second story about the March sisters, Meg, Jo, Beth, and Amy and their friend Laurie as each grows from childhood into adulthood. Life promises adventures, fulfillment and painful trials along the way, marriage, disappointment in love and a tragedy which touches them all, each of them finally finds happiness, if not always in the way they expect.', NULL, 'English', '1870-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12147640-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13165461-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16894032W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (196, NULL, 'The Legend of Sleepy Hollow', '{}', '2026-01-25 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A superstitious schoolmaster, in love with a wealthy farmer''s daughter, has a terrifying encounter with a headless horseman.', NULL, 'English', '1820-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243083-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9856530-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL63985W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (197, NULL, 'The Alhambra', '{}', '2026-01-25 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Verhalen over het gebouwencomplex in Granada, dat eigendom was van de laatste islamitische vorsten in Spanje.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8237030-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5736994-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL63996W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (198, NULL, 'Rip Van Winkle and Sleepy Hollow', '{}', '2026-01-25 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'In the first of these stories from the Catskill Mountains, a superstitious schoolmaster encounters a headless horseman; in the second, a man sleeps for twenty years, waking to a much-changed world.', NULL, 'English', '1867-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8999022-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6291100-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL63877W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (199, NULL, 'Life of George Washington', '{}', '2026-01-25 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Originally published in five volumes between 1853 and 1859, it is a treasure chest of information on Washington and the Civil War. This work is presumeably the most intimate and fascinating biography of a man who worked his way from an Army commander to the first President of the United States.', NULL, 'English', '1850-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243153-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL63991W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (200, NULL, 'Rip Van Winkle', '{}', '2026-01-25 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-25 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, '1891 edition,g.p.putnam,a legendof the kaatskill mountains, by washington irving, fiction', NULL, 'English', '1850-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8241453-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL63995W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (201, NULL, 'Rip Van Winkle and Other Stories', '{}', '2026-01-26 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The legendary enchantment of Rip Van Winkle in the Kaatskill Mountains; the gruesome end of Ichabod Crane, who met the headless horseman of Sleepy Hollow; the spectre bridegroom who turned out to be happily substantial; the pride of an English village and the come-uppance of the over-zealous Mountjoy - these witty, perceptive and captivating tales range from fantasy to romance.', NULL, 'English', '1922-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/102182-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL6043018W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (202, NULL, 'Cuentos clásicos del norte', '{}', '2026-01-26 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Cuentos clásicos del norte, by Washington Irving.', NULL, 'English', '1920-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10226167-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14876294W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (203, NULL, 'A history of New York', '{}', '2026-01-26 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A history of New York : from the beginning of the world to the end of the Dutch dynasty ; containing, among many surprising and curious matters, the unutterable ponderings of Walter the Doubter, the disastrous projects of William the Testy, and the chivalric achievements of Peter the Headstrong ; the three Dutch governors of New Amsterdam ; being the only authentic history of the times that ever hath been or ever will be published.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1991009-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242966-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL63871W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (204, NULL, 'The sketch-book of Geoffrey Crayon, Esq', '{}', '2026-01-26 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Sketch Book of Geoffrey Crayon is the compilation of 34 short stories and essays by Washington Irving. It includes some of his most famous stories, such as The Legend of Sleepy Hollow and Rip Van Winkle, and was one of the first works of American fiction to become popular in Britain and Europe. The tone of the stories varies widely, and they are held together by the powerful charm of their narrator, Geoffrey Crayon.', NULL, 'English', '1819-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7162030-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5646348-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL63893W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (205, NULL, 'Astoria', '{}', '2026-01-26 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'In 1811 a group of American traders built a fort at the mouth of the Columbia River, named Fort Astoria in honor of its financier, John Jacob Astor. Envisioned as the spur of a fur-trading empire, by 1813 the project was a business failure and the fort was surrendered to the British. But in its short life Astoria rendered incalculable benefits to public understanding of the Great Northwest. The exploration of trade routes, the description of various Indian tribes and their customs, and an American claim on the Northwest coast were among many of its legacies.\n\nAstor never relinquished his pride in the enterprise and insisted that the West would one day be a dominating factor in national politics. To drive his point home he asked Washington Irving, the country\'s most renowned and respected author, to transform the papers of Fort Astoria into a unified and readable history.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/448955-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5577201-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL63862W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (206, NULL, 'The Last of the Mohicans', '{}', '2026-01-26 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The classic tale of Hawkeye — Natty Bumppo — the frontier scout who turned his back on "civilization," and his friendship with a Mohican warrior as they escort two sisters through the dangerous wilderness of Indian country in frontier America.', NULL, 'English', '1826-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8236937-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5901135-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL77958W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Last_of_the_Mohicans}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (207, NULL, 'The deerslayer', '{}', '2026-01-26 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Deerslayer is the last book in Cooper''s Leatherstocking Tales pentalogy, but acts as a prequel to the other novels. It begins with the rapid civilizing of New York, in which surrounds the following books take place. It introduces the hero of the Tales, Natty Bumppo, and his philosophy that every living thing should follow its own nature. He is contrasted to other, less conscientious, frontiersmen.', NULL, 'English', '1841-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8237593-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1837566-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL77950W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (208, NULL, 'The Pathfinder', '{}', '2026-01-26 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Vigorous, self-reliant, amazingly resourceful, and moral, Natty Bumppo is the prototype of the Western hero. A faultless arbiter of wilderness justice, he hates middle-class hypocrisy. But he finds his love divided between the woman he has pledged to protect on a treacherous journey and the untouched forest that sustains him in his beliefs. A fast-paced narrative full of adventure and majestic descriptions of early frontier life, Indian raiders, and defenseless outposts, The Pathfinder set the standard for epic action literature.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8980913-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8241435-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL78009W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (209, NULL, 'The Prairie', '{}', '2026-01-26 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Deep in the heart of the newly acquired Louisiana Purchase, five hundred miles beyond the Mississippi River, a group of travelers in the year 1805 pushes yet farther westward over the prairie. Called "squatters" and equipped with covered wagons, livestock, farming implements, and household furnishings, they give every appearance of being ordinary settlers except for the fact they have bypassed the fertile river bottoms for the less productive Great Plains. This group is comprised of the rough, semiliterate Ishmael and Esther Bush, now in their fifties; their numerous children, including seven grown sons; Esther''s brother, Abiram White; Ellen Wade, a niece, whose bearing bespeaks a more refined background; and Dr. Obed Bat, an eccentric naturalist. In search of a camping place for the night, they are suddenly confronted by a colossal figure who momentarily fills them with superstitious awe. It is Natty Bumppo, whose form, greatly magnified by an optical illusion, is outlined against the setting sun on the horizon.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5578106-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6054179-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL77970W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (210, NULL, 'The pioneers', '{}', '2026-01-26 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-26 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'MEET NATTY BUMPPO The first volume in the famous Leatherstocking Tales, The Pioneers introduces Natty Bumppo, the quintessential American hunter and frontiersman who struggles to defend his cherished freedom.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9000512-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/295504-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL77997W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pioneers_(novel)}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (211, NULL, 'The spy', '{}', '2026-01-27 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Inspired by accusations of venality leveled at the men who captured Major Andre (Benedict Arnold''s co-conspirator, executed for espionage in 1780), Cooper''s novel centers on Harry Birch, a common man wrongly suspected by well-born Patriots of being a spy for the British. Even George Washington, who supports Birch, misreads the man, and when Washington offers him payment for information vital to the Patriot''s cause, Birch scorns the money and asserts that his action were motivated not by financial reward, but by his devotion to the fight for independence. A historical adventure tale reminiscent of Sir Walter Scott''s Waverley novels, The Spy is also a parable of the American experience, a reminder that the nation''s survival, like its Revolution, depends on judging people by their actions, not their class or reputations.', NULL, 'English', '1821-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8245225-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5994064-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL78075W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (212, NULL, 'Sea Tales', '{}', '2026-01-27 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'An American frigate and her supporting schooner enter a shoal-filled bay off Northumberland (northeastern England) on a bleak day in December during the American Revolution. Their immediate purpose is to pick up from the rocky cliffs someone referred to at first simply as a pilot. There is a suggestion that he may be a very special pilot when Captain Munson, commander of the frigate, orders his first officer, Lieutenant Edward Griffith, to stand offshore in the ship''s barge, filled with marines, while Lieutenant Richard Barnstable, commander of the schooner Ariel, goes ashore in a whaleboat with a handful of men to bring off the stranger.', NULL, 'English', '1823-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1876696-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7211198-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL77972W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (213, NULL, 'The water-witch', '{}', '2026-01-27 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The water-witch, by James Fenimore Cooper.', NULL, 'English', '1830-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1846352-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5648240-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL78052W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (214, NULL, 'The Red Rover', '{}', '2026-01-27 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'In "The Red Rover," a notorious pirate is chased by a disguised agent of the Royal Navy. Romance, adventure, political intrigue, revelations of mistaken identity--here is Cooper at his best: a painter of brilliant seascapes, a riveting narrator of suspense.\n--- The Library of America', NULL, 'English', '1827-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5742734-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8980910-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL77998W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (215, NULL, 'Precaution', '{}', '2026-01-27 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The entire focus of this novel rests on the determined though sometimes woefully mistaken efforts of three British families--the Moseleys, the Jarvises, and the Chattertons--to arrange suitable marriages for their respective sons and daughters. The bulk of the early-nineteenth-century action is therefore played out through dinners, social calls, visits to summer resorts, and development of various designs employed toward the end of matrimony. The "precaution" displayed by Mrs. Wilson in guiding her niece Emily Moseley through the treacherous shoals toward a sound Christian marriage furnishes the novel''s title and indicates the author''s moral and ethical position.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5678531-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2897834-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL78069W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (216, NULL, 'The Moonstone', '{}', '2026-01-27 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'One of the first English detective novels, this mystery involves the disappearance of a valuable diamond, originally stolen from a Hindu idol, given to a young woman on her eighteenth birthday, and then stolen again. A classic of 19th-century literature.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8237041-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1053016-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL176092W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilkie_Collins}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (217, NULL, 'The Woman in White', '{}', '2026-01-27 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Woman in White famously opens with Walter Hartright''s eerie encounter on a moonlit London road. Engaged as a drawing master to the beautiful Laura Fairlie, Walter is drawn into the sinister intrigues of Sir Percival Glyde and his ''charming'' friend Count Fosco, who has a taste for white mice, vanilla bonbons and poison. Pursuing questions of identity and insanity along the paths and corridors of English country houses and the madhouse, The Woman in White is the first and most influential of the Victorian genre that combined Gothic horror with psychological realism.', NULL, 'English', '1859-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4684227-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8235282-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL176045W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (218, NULL, 'The Haunted Hotel', '{}', '2026-01-27 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'This is perhaps Collins'' last lucid effort before ill health and opium drained his powers. A tale of ghostly terror, relentless pace, tight narrative, and a doomed Countess characterize and distinguish this powerful Collins novelette.', NULL, 'English', '1878-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2890291-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242771-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL176025W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (219, NULL, 'Armadale', '{}', '2026-01-27 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Cuando el anciano Allan Armadale escribe su terrible confesión en el lecho de muerte, no puede ni imaginarse las repercusiones que tendrá esa carta cuando su hijo recién nacido la lea años después. Por segunda vez, dos hombres con el mismo nombre y el mismo apellido se verán implicados en la prosecución de una herencia que parece maldita. Mientras tanto, se suceden las sigilosas intrigas de Lydia Gwilt, un personaje misterioso y perverso que horrorizó a los lectores victorianos y que todavía hoy sobrecoge. Una mujer que llegó a ser definida por la crítica como "una de las villanas más curtidas". Con estos hilos y la complicidad del lector, el maestro Wilkie Collins teje una trama envolvente y seductora que brega entre identidades confusas, maldiciones heredadas, rivalidades amorosas, espionaje… y asesinatos.', NULL, 'English', '1866-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/780215-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/119225-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL176085W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (220, NULL, 'No name', '{}', '2026-01-27 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-27 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'No Name is a 19th-century novel by the master of sensation fiction, Wilkie Collins. A country gentleman is killed in an accident and his wife dies shortly after him. The blow is double for their daughters, who discover that they were born before their parents were married. Their sudden illegitimacy robs them of their inheritance and their accustomed place in society.', NULL, 'English', '1862-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/103261-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8245183-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL176090W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (221, NULL, 'No Thoroughfare', '{}', '2026-01-28 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'No Thoroughfare, by Wilkie Collins.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1844225-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13704167-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL9253342W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (222, NULL, 'The dead secret', '{}', '2026-01-28 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The dead secret, by Wilkie Collins.', NULL, 'English', '1857-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14305247-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11967308-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL176087W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (223, NULL, 'Hide and seek, or, The mystery of Mary Grice', '{}', '2026-01-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A mystery unfolds around a deaf and mute girl named Mary, or Madonna adopted by artist Valentine Blyth, whose true identity and family history are shrouded in secrets, leading to a search for her origins and a revelation of a long-hidden family scandal.', NULL, 'English', '1854-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/309703-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/119407-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL176054W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (224, NULL, 'Blind love', '{}', '2026-01-28 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Blind love, by Wilkie Collins.', NULL, 'English', '1889-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/310188-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11337142-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL176062W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (225, NULL, 'The Guilty River', '{}', '2026-01-28 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Guilty River, by Wilkie Collins.', NULL, 'English', '1886-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5723048-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5998217-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL176066W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (226, NULL, 'Barchester Towers', '{}', '2026-01-28 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'The Chronicles of Barsetshire, Book 2: Barchester Towers \n\nWritten as a sequel to "The Warden", this is the second book of the Barsetshire novels. Described as humorous, this wonderful novel that interweaves power, love, greed, and deceit in Barchester. \n\nBarchester Towers (1857) is the second of the six Chronicles of Barsetshire, the work in which, after a ten-year apprenticeship, Trollope finally found his distinctive voice. In this his most popular novel, the chronicler continues the story of Mr. Harding and his daughter Eleanor, begun in The Warden, adding to his cast of characters that oily symbol of "progress" Mr. Slope, the hen-pecked Dr. Proudie, and the amiable and breezy Stanhope family. Love, mammon, clerical in-fighting, and promotion again figure prominently and comically, all centered on the magnificently imagined cathedral city of Barchester.', NULL, 'English', '1815-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1468666-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/127135-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109724W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (227, NULL, 'The Warden', '{}', '2026-01-28 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'The Chronicles of Barsetshire, Book 1: The Warden\n\nThe tranquil atmosphere of the cathedral town of Barchester is shattered when a scandal breaks concerning the financial affairs of a Church-run almshouse for elderly men. In the ensuing furore, Septimus Harding, the almshouse\'s well-meaning warden, finds himself pitted against his daughter\'s suitor Dr John Bold, a zealous local reformer. Matters are not improved when Harding\'s abrasive son-in law, Archdeacon Grantly, leaps into the fray to defend him against a campaign Bold begins in the national press. An affectionate and wittily satirical view of the workings of the Church of England, The Warden, the first of the Barchester Chronicles, is also a subtle exploration of the rights and wrongs of moral crusades and, in its account of Harding\'s intensely felt personal drama, a moving depiction of the private impact of public affairs.', NULL, 'English', '1809-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8238730-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/539789-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109882W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (228, NULL, 'Framley Parsonage', '{}', '2026-01-28 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'The Chronicles of Barsetshire, Book 4: Framley Parsonage \n\nWhen young Mark Robarts was leaving college, his father might well declare that all men began to say all good things to him, and to extol his fortune in that he had a son blessed with an excellent disposition. This father was a physician living at Exeter. He was a gentleman possessed of no private means, but enjoying a lucrative practice, which had enabled him to maintain and educate a family with all the advantages which money can give in this country.', NULL, 'English', '1861-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8288051-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/3005653-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109880W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (229, NULL, 'The three clerks', '{}', '2026-01-28 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Set in the 1850s, The Three Clerks exposes and probes the relationships between three clerks and the three sisters who became their wives. At the same time it satirizes the Civil Service examinations and financial corruption in dealings on the stock market.', NULL, 'English', '1858-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9063811-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5904504-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109875W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (230, NULL, 'Cousin Henry', '{}', '2026-01-28 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-28 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When the Squire of Llanfeare dies, his nephew Henry inherits the estate. Rumours are rife that the Squire had named his niece Isabel as his heir, and that Henry is an impostor. Mr Apjohn, the family lawyer, takes it upon himself to investigate.', NULL, 'English', '1879-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/118353-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9179498-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109843W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (231, NULL, 'An eye for an eye', '{}', '2026-01-29 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'An eye for an eye, by Anthony Trollope.', NULL, 'English', '1879-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/756392-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10386811-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109863W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (232, NULL, 'The way we live now', '{}', '2026-01-29 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'From a review of the Anthony Trollope canon in The Economist (2020/04/08 edition):\n*“The Way We Live Now” (1875) is as much a portrait of the last few decades as it is of the high Victorian age, and every bit as addictive as HBO’s hit series “Succession”. The novel’s anti-hero, Augustus Melmotte, is one of the great portraits of the businessman as ogre — a “horrid, big, rich scoundrel”, “a bloated swindler” and “vile city ruffian” who bears an uncanny resemblance to the late Robert Maxwell (and to living figures who had best not be named for legal reasons). Despite his foreign birth and mysterious past, Melmotte forces his way into British society by playing on the greed of bigwigs who despise him yet compete for his favours. He buys his way into the House of Commons; he floats a railway company that is ostensibly designed to build a line between Mexico and America but is really a paper scheme for selling shares.', NULL, 'English', '1875-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8246152-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13075659-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109871W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (233, NULL, 'Doctor Thorne', '{}', '2026-01-29 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'The Chronicles of Barsetshire, Book 3: Dr. Thorne \n\nMary Thorne, orphaned (and illegitimate) niece of Dr. Thorne, has long been a favorite at Greshamsbury House--until Lady Arabella Gresham learns that her only son Frank is in love with Mary. The unhappy Mary is banished forthwith, because the Gresham family fortunes are so depleted that Frank must marry money.\n\nFrank, however, is one of the few completely honorable young men in Trollope\'s novels and remains stubbornly true to his love. Well, he does propose to another woman, at the insistence of his mother, but only with the virtual certainty that he will be rejected--as indeed he is. The lady is Miss Dunstable, one of Trollope\'s most delightful characters, a fabulously wealthy thirtyish heiress of an ointment company. She is a bold, witty woman, not beautiful, but attractive in her way, whose wealth invites countless proposals.\nAfter the rather complicated plot unfolds, the tables are completely turned, and Mary is eagerly welcomed by Lady Arabella (who, of course, has always loved her) as the savior of the family.', NULL, 'English', '1858-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6817399-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/297961-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109881W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (234, NULL, 'Harry Heathcote of Gangoil', '{}', '2026-01-29 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Harry Heathcote is a young immigrant “squatter,” farming thousands of acres in Queensland, Australia. His strong personality wins the loyalty of friends and family. But that same imperious nature makes him enemies, too, who would like nothing more than to see him ruined. As Christmas approaches, the conditions for his ruin arise naturally in the intense, scorching heat of a southern hemisphere summer. His enemies, however, spot an opportunity to give nature a helping hand. Their sharp conflict contrasts with a muted romantic subplot — but even here, Heathcote’s tone and temper complicate the path of true love. An invitation to produce a “Christmas story” came while Anthony Trollope was writing The Way We Live Now . Harry Heathcote was the result, fulfilling the brief, but without the “humbug” that Trollope believed marred too much writing in that genre. Harry Heathcote is one of Trollope’s shorter novels, but still displays his sharp psychological insight into his leading characters, and his capacity to produce natural dialog.', NULL, 'English', '1874-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/118788-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9178063-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109866W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (235, NULL, 'The Eustace diamonds', '{}', '2026-01-29 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Palliser Novels, book 3: The Eustace Diamonds', NULL, 'English', '1872-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242844-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14154523-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL109873W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (236, NULL, 'Tess of the d''Urbervilles', '{}', '2026-01-29 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'An intimate portrait of a woman, one of literature''s most admirable and tragic heroines...Tess Durbeyfield knows what it is to work hard and expect little. But her life is about to veer from the path trod by her mother and grandmother. When her ne''er-do-well father learns that his family is the last of a long noble line, the d''Urbervilles, he sends Tess on a journey to meet her supposed kin — a journey that will see her victimized by lust, poverty, and hypocrisy. Shaped by an acute sense of social injustice and by a vision of human fate cosmic in scope, her story is a singular blending of harsh realism and poignant beauty. Thomas Hardy created in Tess not a standard Victorian heroine but a woman whose intense vitality shines against the bleak backdrop of a dying way of life. The novel shocked contemporary readers with its honesty and remains a timeless commentary on the human condition.', NULL, 'English', '1707-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13109386-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13109110-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL44927W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (237, NULL, 'The Mayor of Casterbridge', '{}', '2026-01-29 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Like many of Hardy’s novels, The Mayor of Casterbridge is set in the fictional county of Wessex in the mid 1800s. It begins with Michael Henchard, a young hay-trusser, drunk on rum, auctioning off his wife and baby daughter at a village fair. The next day, overcome with remorse, Henchard resolves to turn his life around. When we meet Henchard eighteen years later, temperance and hard work have made him wealthy and respectable. However, he cannot escape his past. His secret guilt, his pride, and his impulsive temper all serve to sabotage his good name. \n The Mayor of Casterbridge was published in 1886, first as a magazine serial and then later that year as a book. It is perhaps most noteworthy for the psychological portrait of Michael Henchard, a tragic character who remains sympathetic while simultaneously being deeply flawed. Typical of other Hardy novels, it also vividly depicts life in the rural countryside at that time.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1260617-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6818897-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL8193406W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (238, NULL, 'Jude the Obscure', '{}', '2026-01-29 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Hardy''s last work of fiction, Jude the Obscure is also one of his most gloomily fatalistic, depicting the lives of individuals who are trapped by forces beyond their control. Jude Fawley, a poor villager, wants to enter the divinity school at Christminster. Sidetracked by Arabella Donn, an earthy country girl who pretends to be pregnant by him, Jude marries her and is then deserted. He earns a living as a stonemason at Christminster; there he falls in love with his independent-minded cousin, Sue Bridehead. Out of a sense of obligation, Sue marries the schoolmaster Phillotson, who has helped her. Unable to bear living with Phillotson, she returns to live with Jude and eventually bears his children out of wedlock. Their poverty and the weight of society''s disapproval begin to take a toll on Sue and Jude; the climax occurs when Jude''s son by Arabella hangs Sue and Jude''s children and himself. In penance, Sue returns to Phillotson and the church. Jude returns to Arabella and eventually dies miserably.', NULL, 'English', '1895-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12973053-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL44986W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (239, NULL, 'Under the Greenwood Tree or, The Mellstock quire', '{}', '2026-01-29 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Under the Greenwood Tree is the story of the romantic entanglement between church musician, Dick Dewey, and the attractive new school mistress, Fancy Day. A pleasant romantic tale set in the Victorian era, Under the Greenwood Tree is one of Thomas Hardy''s most gentle and pastoral novels.', NULL, 'English', '1872-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/902186-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/103379-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL44973W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (240, NULL, 'The Woodlanders', '{}', '2026-01-29 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-29 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When country-girl Grace Melbury returns home from her middle-class school she feels she has risen above her suitor, the simple woodsman Giles Winterborne. Though marriage had been discussed between her and Giles, Grace finds herself captivated by Dr Edred Fitzpiers, a sophisticated newcomer to the area - a relationship that is encouraged by her socially ambitious father. Hardy''s novel of betrayal, disillusionment and moral compromise depicts a secluded community coming to terms with the disastrous impact of outside influences. And in his portrayal of Giles Winterborne, Hardy shows a man who responds deeply to the forces of the natural world, thought they ultimately betray him.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243078-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6057445-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL44990W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (241, NULL, 'Far from the Madding Crowd', '{}', '2026-01-30 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Independent and spirited Bathsheba Everdene has come to Weatherbury to take up her position as a farmer on the largest estate in the area. Her bold presence draws three very different suitors: the gentleman-farmer Boldwood, soldier-seducer Sergeant Troy and the devoted shepherd Gabriel Oak. Each, in contrasting ways, unsettles her decisions and complicates her life, and tragedy ensues, threatening the stability of the whole community. The first of his works set in the fictional county of Wessex, Hardy''s novel of swift passion and slow courtship is imbued with his evocative descriptions of rural life and landscapes, and with unflinching honesty about sexual relationships.', NULL, 'English', '1874-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/902038-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8237658-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL44995W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (242, NULL, 'The Return of the Native', '{}', '2026-01-30 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The native of the title is Clym Yeobright, who returns to the area from the bright society of Paris and, as any reader of Hardy knows, all is not smooth. He is quickly taken by and marries the one woman he should not--Eustacia Vye. The suffering that follows is mitigated somewhat by the ending.', NULL, 'English', '1878-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8162989-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6558144-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL44994W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (243, NULL, 'Moments of vision', '{}', '2026-01-30 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'ix, 443 p. ; 23 cm', NULL, 'English', '1889-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5806149-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL44912W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (244, NULL, 'The Trumpet-Major, and Robert His Brother', '{}', '2026-01-30 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Set against a backdrop of the Napoleonic wars, this is a novel about a young woman and the three very different suitors who vie for her hand. Two of the men are brothers involved in the fighting, one an easygoing sailor, the other an honest and diffident trumpet major, the third suitor being the cowardly son of the local squire.', NULL, 'English', '1880-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242138-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2505348-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL44993W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (245, NULL, 'The well-beloved', '{}', '2026-01-30 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Jocelyn Pierston, a sculptor of growing fame, is determined to find his ideal in womanhood, a quest that has led to many fruitless encounters. For just as it seems he has found his heart''s desire, disillusionment sets in and his burning love turns to ashes. Returning to Portland, his birthplace, he meets young, innocent Avice Caro. They are betrothed until a fateful meeting with the self-assured Marcia Bencomb changes the course of his life yet again. Please Note: This book is easy to read in true text, not scanned images that can sometimes be difficult to decipher. The Microsoft eBook has a contents page linked to the chapter headings for easy navigation. The Adobe eBook has bookmarks at chapter headings and is printable up to two full copies per year. Both versions are text searchable.', NULL, 'English', '1897-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242184-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL44989W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (246, NULL, 'The Mill on the Floss', '{}', '2026-01-30 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'From the author of MIDDLEMARCH and SILAS MARNER, a story of frustrated intelligence and longing, featuring the intelligent Maggie, who yearns to be loved, and her brother Tom, who is forced to study. When Maggie is cast out by Tom, she is ostracized by society, and must face the consequences of renunciation.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8236884-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1900122-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20938W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (247, NULL, 'Silas Marner', '{}', '2026-01-30 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Eliot''s touching novel of a miser and a little child combines the charm of a fairy tale with the humor and pathos of realistic fiction. The gentle linen weaver, Silas Marner, exiles himself to the town of Raveloe after being falsely accused of a heinous theft. There he begins to find redemption and spiritual rebirth through his unselfish love for an abandoned child he discovers in his isolated cottage.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9286405-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1922001-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20874W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (248, NULL, 'Adam Bede', '{}', '2026-01-30 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Adam Bede is a hardy young carpenter who cares for his aging mother. His one weakness is the woman he loves blindly: the trifling town beauty, Hetty Sorrel, whose only delights are her baubles-and the delusion that the careless Captain Donnithorne may ask for her hand. Betrayed by their innocence, both Adam and Hetty allow their foolish hearts to trap them in a triangle of seduction, murder, and retribution.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6379692-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4817408-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20935W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (249, NULL, 'Middlemarch', '{}', '2026-01-30 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Eliot’s epic of 19th century provincial social life, set in a fictitious Midlands town in the years 1830-32, has several interlocking storylines blended effortlessly together to form a fully coherent narrative. Its main themes are the status of women, social expectations and hypocrisy, religion, political reform and education. It has often been called the greatest novel in the English language.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/252882-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/295293-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20867W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (250, NULL, 'Felix Holt, the radical', '{}', '2026-01-30 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-30 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Two men vying for the hand of Esther, a young woman of charm and virtue, are Felix Holt, an idealistic young artisan, and Harold Transome, the intelligent heir to an estate. She is drawn to Holt yet has dreams of marrying into a life of refinement.', NULL, 'English', '1777-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8277137-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242851-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20932W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (251, NULL, 'Daniel Deronda', '{}', '2026-01-31 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'As Daniel Deronda opens, Gwendolen Harleth is poised at the roulette-table, prepared to throw away her family fortune. She is observed by Daniel Deronda, a young man groomed in the finest tradition of the English upper-classes. And while Gwendolen loses everything and becomes trapped in an oppressive marriage, Deronda''s fortunes take a different turn. After a dramatic encounter with the young Jewish woman Mirah, he becomes involved in a search for her lost family and finds himself drawn into ever-deeper sympathies with Jewish aspirations and identity. ''I meant everything in the book to be related to everything else'', wrote George Eliot of her last and most ambitious novel, and in weaving her plot strands together she created a bold and richly textured picture of British society and the Jewish experience within it.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243960-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20933W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (252, NULL, 'Romola', '{}', '2026-01-31 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Eliot’s only historical novel, set in 15th century Florence under the rule of the Medicis, blends fact with fiction as the reader follows the almost saint-like Romola and the amoral and feckless Tito Melema whom she marries against the advice of her brother, an equally saintly priest. An impressive account of Renaissance life in a wealthy Italian state.', NULL, 'English', '1863-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/297937-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8244511-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20936W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (253, NULL, 'Scenes of clerical life', '{}', '2026-01-31 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Scenes of clerical life, by George Eliot.', NULL, 'English', '1858-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242346-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15856643W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (254, NULL, 'Impressions of Theophrastus Such', '{}', '2026-01-31 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"Impressions of Theophrastus Such, published in 1879, marks the end of George Eliot''s career and the end of her life with George Henry Lewes. In many ways this fable is a final testimony to her brilliance, and yet it is puzzling that it has traditionally been judged as inferior to her other works. It remains, on the contrary, a significant reflection of her earlier works and an experiment apart from them." "As Nancy Henry points out in her comprehensive introduction, this book goes beyond even Daniel Deronda in positing the role of collective memory in the future of national cultures and the power of literary texts in creating and preserving both. It is a complex and deeply intelligent synthesis of Eliot''s previous great works as well as an interesting departure from them.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5743995-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20930W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (255, NULL, 'The Spanish gypsy', '{}', '2026-01-31 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Spanish gypsy, by George Eliot.', NULL, 'English', '1868-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4807882-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20929W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (256, NULL, 'The Duel and Other Stories [8 stories]', '{}', '2026-01-31 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Contains:\nАптекарша\nВ родном углу\nДорогие уроки\nДуэль\nКнягиня\nСоседи\nТина\nХорошие люди', NULL, 'Russian', '1984-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12748259-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8294964-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL278134W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (257, NULL, 'The Chorus Girl and Other Stories [12 stories]', '{}', '2026-01-31 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Contains:\nМоя жизнь', NULL, 'Russian', '1985-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13657763-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL55512W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (258, NULL, 'The schoolmaster and other stories', '{}', '2026-01-31 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'From the book:FYODOR LUKITCH SYSOEV, the master of the factory school maintained at the expense of the firm of Kulikin, was getting ready for the annual dinner. Every year after the school examination the board of managers gave a dinner at which the inspector of elementary schools, all who had conducted the examinations, and all the managers and foremen of the factory were present. In spite of their official character, these dinners were always good and lively, and the guests sat a long time over them; forgetting distinc-tions of rank and recalling only their meritorious labours, they ate till they were full, drank amicably, chattered till they were all hoarse and parted late in the evening, deafening the whole factory settlement with their singing and the sound of their kisses. Of such dinners Sysoev had taken part in thirteen, as he had been that number of years master of the factory school.', NULL, 'Russian', '1986-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12752377-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL55438W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (259, NULL, 'The House With The Mezzanine and Other Stories [7 stories]', '{}', '2026-01-31 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Contains:\nМоя жизнь', NULL, 'Russian', '2007-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14016669-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2501213-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL278135W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (260, NULL, 'The bet and other stories [13 stories]', '{}', '2026-01-31 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-01-31 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The bet and other stories [13 stories], by Anton Chekhov.', NULL, 'Russian', '1915-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12749852-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5565849-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL55455W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (261, NULL, 'The Black Monk and other stories [12 stories]', '{}', '2026-02-01 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Chekhov\'s pages are peopled with psychopaths, degenerates of genius and virtue and satirically comic characters who succumb in feeble revolt against the baseness and banality of life. They are quite unfit to combat the healthy, rude, but unintelligent forces around them.\n\nKovrin, Likhary6ff and Dr Andréi Yéfimitch, three heroes in this collection, are characteristic of Chekhov\'s outlook. Andréi Vasilyevitch Kovrin, the chief char- acter in the title story, had worn himself out and unsettled his nerves. His doctor advised him to spend the spring and summer in the country and in the nick of time came a long letter from Tänya Pesötsky asking him to•come and stay with her father at Borisovka. It was a journey which was to lead to marriage, madness and death. With the other stories and characters in this collection we have the best of Chekhov.', NULL, 'Russian', '1903-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12818720-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL55490W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (262, NULL, 'The Lady with the Dog and Other Stories [9 stories]', '{}', '2026-02-01 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'From the book:\nIT was said that a new person had appeared on the sea-front: a lady with a little dog. Dmitri Dmitritch Gurov, who had by then been a fortnight at Yalta, and so was fairly at home there, had begun to take an interest in new arrivals. Sitting in Verney\'s pavilion, he saw, walking on the sea-front, a fair-haired young lady of medium height, wearing a beret; a white Pomeranian dog was running behind her. And afterwards he met her in the public gardens and in the square several times a day. She was walking alone, always wearing the same beret, and always with the same white dog; no one knew who she was, and every one called her simply "the lady with the dog."', NULL, 'Russian', '1984-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12749981-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL278145W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (263, NULL, 'The witch and other stories [15 stories]', '{}', '2026-02-01 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The witch and other stories [15 stories], by Anton Chekhov.', NULL, 'Russian', '1985-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12768930-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL55511W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (264, NULL, 'The Bishop and Other Stories [7 stories]', '{}', '2026-02-01 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Short story collection containing:\nСтепь', NULL, 'Russian', '1985-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12749979-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL55523W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (265, NULL, 'Note-Book of Anton Chekhov', '{}', '2026-02-01 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Contains Chekhov''s diary from 1896, the text of his notebooks from the years 1892 to 1904 that contain ideas for future works and quotations that he liked, and a collection of themes, thoughts, notes, and fragments.', NULL, 'Russian', '1921-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'Russian Empire', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12750020-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL55496W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (266, NULL, 'Bel-Ami', '{}', '2026-02-01 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, '.I Quand la caissiere lui eut rendu la monnaie de sa piece de cent sous, Georges Duroy sortit du restaurant. Comme il portait beau, par nature et par pose d''ancien sous-officier, il cambra sa taille, frisa sa moustache d''un geste militaire et familier, et jeta sur les dineurs attardes un regard rapide et circulaire, un de ces regards de joli garcon qui s''etendent comme des coups d''epervier. Les femmes avaient leve la tete vers lui, trois petites ouvrieres, une maitresse de musique entre deux ages, mal peignee, negligee, coiffee d''un chapeau toujours poussiereux et vetue d''une robe toujours de travers, et deux bourgeoises avec leurs maris, habituees de cette gargote a prix fixe. Lorsqu''il fut sur le trottoir, il demeura un instant immobile se demandant ce qu''il allait faire. On etait au 28 juin, et il lui restait juste en poche trois francs quarante pour finir le mois. Cela representait deux diners sans dejeuners, ou deux dejeuners sans diners, au choix.', NULL, 'French', '1893-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/997432-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8235348-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL93842W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (267, NULL, 'Pierre et Jean', '{}', '2026-02-01 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Pierre et Jean is a naturalist or psycho-realist work written by Guy de Maupassant in Étretat in his native Normandy between June and September 1887 . This was Maupassant’s shortest novel. It appeared in three instalments in the Nouvelle Revue and then in volume form in 1888, together with the essay “Le Roman”. Pierre et Jean is a realist work, notably so by the subjects on which it treats, including knowledge of one''s heredity (whether one is a legitimate son or a bastard), the bourgeoisie, and the problems stemming from money.', NULL, 'French', '1887-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8245172-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL93841W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (268, NULL, 'Boule de suif', '{}', '2026-02-01 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, '432 p', NULL, 'French', '1899-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/979880-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7173992-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15304774W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (269, NULL, 'Le Horla', '{}', '2026-02-01 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Le Horla, by Guy de Maupassant.', NULL, 'French', '1887-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4859675-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16246207W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (270, NULL, 'Mademoiselle Fifi', '{}', '2026-02-01 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-01 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The title story of this collection is, like many of the others, set during the Franco-Prussian war. As in so many of Maupassant’s stories he explores class barriers and looks at the contrasts between the French and German combatants.', NULL, 'French', '1882-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6468088-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL93833W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (271, NULL, 'Une vie', '{}', '2026-02-02 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Included in this volume are A Woman''s Life, Hautot Senior and Hautot Junior, Little Louise Roque, and 8 more tales.', NULL, 'French', '1883-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6866195-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL93840W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (272, NULL, 'The odd number', '{}', '2026-02-02 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The odd number, by Guy de Maupassant.', NULL, 'French', '1889-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8245374-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL93839W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (273, NULL, 'Mont-Oriol', '{}', '2026-02-02 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Mont-Oriol, by Guy de Maupassant.', NULL, 'French', '1886-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6541255-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL93838W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (274, NULL, 'Short stories', '{}', '2026-02-02 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Short stories, by Guy de Maupassant.', NULL, 'French', '1893-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242807-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16246212W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (275, NULL, 'Fort comme la mort', '{}', '2026-02-02 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Fort comme la mort, by Guy de Maupassant.', NULL, 'French', '1889-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6502133-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL93835W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (276, NULL, 'The Devil''s Dictionary', '{}', '2026-02-02 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Devil''s Dictionary was begun in a weekly paper in 1881, and was continued in a desultory way at long intervals until 1906. In that year a large part of it was published in covers with the title The Cynic''s Word Book, a name which the author had not the power to reject or happiness to approve. To quote the publishers of the present work: "This more reverent title had previously been forced upon him by the religious scruples of the last newspaper in which a part of the work had appeared, with the natural consequence that when it came out in covers the country already had been flooded by its imitators with a score of ''cynic'' books - The Cynic''s This, The Cynic''s That, and The Cynic''s t''Other. Most of these books were merely stupid, though some of them added the distinction of silliness.', NULL, 'English', '1840-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12671319-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1759022-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7973273W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (277, NULL, 'A Cynic Looks at Life', '{}', '2026-02-02 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A Cynic Looks at Life, by Ambrose Bierce.', NULL, 'English', '1912-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12675113-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2011082-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7973354W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (278, NULL, 'Write It Right', '{}', '2026-02-02 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Write It Right, by Ambrose Bierce.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14388909-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7973344W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (279, NULL, 'In the Midst of Life. Tales of Civilians', '{}', '2026-02-02 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'A collection of 26 stories:\n\nSoldiers (15 stories)\n"A Horseman in the Sky"\nAn Occurrence at Owl Creek Bridge\n"Chickamauga"\n"A Son of the Gods"\n"One of the Missing"\n"Killed at Resaca"\n"The Affair at Coulter\'s Notch"\n"The Coup de Grâce"\n"Parker Adderson, Philosopher"\n"An Affair of Outposts"\n"The Story of a Conscience"\n"One Kind of Officer"\n"One Officer, One Man"\n"George Thurston"\n"The Mocking-Bird"\n\nCivilians (11 stories)\n"The Man Out of the Nose"\n"An Adventure at Brownville"\n"The Famous Gilson Bequest"\n"The Applicant"\nWatcher by the Dead\n"The Man and the Snake"\n"A Holy Terror"\n"The Suitable Surroundings"\n"The Boarded Window"\n"An Heiress from Redhorse"\nThe Eyes of the Panther\n\n----------\nAlso contained in:\n\n - The Best of Ambrose Bierce\n - The Collected Writings of Ambrose Bierce\nDevil’s Dictionary, Tales, & Memoirs', NULL, 'English', '1891-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8753716-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8753594-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7973293W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (280, NULL, 'An Occurrence at Owl Creek Bridge', '{}', '2026-02-02 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-02 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"An Occurrence at Owl Creek Bridge" (1890) is a short story by the American writer and Civil War veteran Ambrose Bierce. Described as "one of the most famous and frequently anthologized stories in American literature", it was originally published by The San Francisco Examiner on July 13, 1890, and was first collected in Bierce''s book Tales of Soldiers and Civilians (1891). The story, which is set during the American Civil War, is known for its irregular time sequence and twist ending. Bierce''s abandonment of strict linear narration in favor of the internal mind of the protagonist is an early example of the stream of consciousness narrative mode.', NULL, 'English', '1980-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12688970-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14863196W,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/An_Occurrence_at_Owl_Creek_Bridge}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (281, NULL, 'Cobwebs from an Empty Skull', '{}', '2026-02-03 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'El tercer libro de Ambrose Bierce, conjunto de fábulas y cuentos en que ya se encuentran todas las características distintivas de su imaginación mordaz, publicado por primera vez al español en edición integral e ilustrada.\nEdición digital.\nISBN: 978-987-28384-7-8', NULL, 'English', '1874-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12670942-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7973355W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (282, NULL, 'The Monk and the Hangman''s Daughter', '{}', '2026-02-03 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Monk and the Hangman''s Daughter, by Ambrose Bierce.', NULL, 'English', '1892-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12676448-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13721092-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL9679346W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (283, NULL, 'Present at a Hanging and Other Ghost Stories', '{}', '2026-02-03 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Present at a Hanging and Other Ghost Stories, by Ambrose Bierce.', NULL, 'English', '1913-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12678357-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7973306W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (284, NULL, 'The Fiend''s Delight', '{}', '2026-02-03 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Fiend''s Delight, by Ambrose Bierce.', NULL, 'English', '1872-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13441464-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7973286W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (285, NULL, 'A Son of the Gods and A Horseman in the Sky', '{}', '2026-02-03 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A Son of the Gods and A Horseman in the Sky, by Ambrose Bierce.', NULL, 'English', '1907-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12671334-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7973320W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (286, NULL, 'The Railway Children', '{}', '2026-02-03 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When Father mysteriously goes away, the children and their mother leave their happy life in London to go and live in a small cottage in the country. ''The Three Chimneys'' lies beside a railway track - a constant source of enjoyment to all three. They make friends with the Station Master and Perks the Porter, as well as the jovial ''Old Gentleman'' who waves to them everyday from the train. But the mystery remains: where is Father, and will he ever return?', NULL, 'English', '1900-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13241123-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/105844-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL99509W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (287, NULL, 'Five Children and It', '{}', '2026-02-03 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Haven''t you ever thought what you would wish for if you were granted three wishes? In Nesbit''s delightful classic, five siblings find a creature that grants their wishes, but as the old saying goes: be careful what you wish for, it might come true...', NULL, 'English', '1905-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/28174-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/118948-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL99499W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (288, NULL, 'The Book of Dragons', '{}', '2026-02-03 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Eight madcap tales of unpredictable dragons — including one made of ice, another that takes refuge in the General Post Office, and a fire-breathing monster that flies out of an enchanted book and eats an entire soccer team! Marvelous adventure and excitement for make-believers of all ages.', NULL, 'English', '1973-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4342323-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/3360546-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL99529W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (289, NULL, 'The Story of the Treasure Seekers', '{}', '2026-02-03 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The six Bastable children try to restore their family''s fortune using a variety of schemes taken from books, including finding buried treasure, rescuing someone from bandits, and starting a newspaper.', NULL, 'English', '1899-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13241364-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/102127-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL99522W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (290, NULL, 'The Story of the Amulet', '{}', '2026-02-03 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-03 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Story of the Amulet, by Edith Nesbit.', NULL, 'English', '1905-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13241470-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/3078455-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL407476W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (291, NULL, 'The Enchanted Castle', '{}', '2026-02-04 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'E. Nesbit''s classic story of how Gerald, Cathy and Jimmy find an enchanted garden and awake a princess from a hundred-year sleep, only to have her immediately made invisible by a magic ring. Her rescue is difficult, funny and sometimes frightening.', NULL, 'English', '1907-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6644514-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243677-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL99541W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (292, NULL, 'The Magic City', '{}', '2026-02-04 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'An extremely unhappy ten-year-old magically escapes into a city he has built out of books, chessmen, candlesticks, and other household items.', NULL, 'English', '1910-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1673063-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/854547-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL99535W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (293, NULL, 'The Phoenix and the Carpet', '{}', '2026-02-04 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Five British children discover in their new carpet an egg, which hatches into a phoenix that takes them on a series of fantastic adventures around the world.', NULL, 'English', '1903-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/902122-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2808728-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL99539W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (294, NULL, 'The Magic World', '{}', '2026-02-04 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Twelve stories with magic occurrences.', NULL, 'English', '1959-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2970137-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8584306-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7984948W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (295, NULL, 'The Wouldbegoods', '{}', '2026-02-04 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Children are like jam: all very well in the proper place, but you can''t stand them all over the shop - eh, what?''', NULL, 'English', '1901-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243273-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2962953-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL99543W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (296, NULL, 'Uncle Tom''s Cabin', '{}', '2026-02-04 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'This unforgettable novel tells the story of Tom, a devoutly Christian slave who chooses not to escape bondage for fear of embarrassing his master. However, he is soon sold to a slave trader and sent down the Mississippi, where he must endure brutal treatment. This is a powerful tale of the extreme cruelties of slavery, as well as the price of loyalty and morality. When first published, it helped to solidify the anti-slavery sentiments of the North, and it remains today as the book that helped move a nation to civil war.\n\n"So this is the little lady who made this big war." Abraham Lincoln\'s legendary comment upon meeting Mrs. Stowe has been seriously questioned, but few will deny that this work fed the passions and prejudices of countless numbers. If it did not "make" the Civil War, it flamed the embers. That Uncle Tom\'s Cabin is far more than an outdated work of propaganda confounds literary criticism. The novel\'s overwhelming power and persuasion have outlived even the most severe of critics.', NULL, 'English', '1850-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12728198-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/247984-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152161W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (297, NULL, 'The pearl of Orr''s Island', '{}', '2026-02-04 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'"The rural tranquillity of the lonely, pine-girthed shores of the Maine coast is the setting for this novel of conflicting aspirations written by one of the most prolific and influential writers in American history. Here is the story of a young girl\'s struggle to belong and fit in, in the face of adversity, and of her upbringing among strong women, grumpy fishermen, annoying gossips, sea captains, and the dreamlike, tempestuous landscape of Orr\'s Island.\n\nThe Pearl of Orr\'s Island is one of the forgotten - but not lost - masterpieces of American literature. It reflects Harriet Beecher Stowe\'s awareness of the complexity of small-town society, her commitment to realism, and her fluency in the local language."--BOOK JACKET.', NULL, 'English', '1862-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/393173-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/767220-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152223W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (298, NULL, 'Queer Little Folks', '{}', '2026-02-04 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Queer Little Folks, by Harriet Beecher Stowe.', NULL, 'English', '1886-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/756617-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2003093-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152211W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (299, NULL, 'Palmetto-leaves', '{}', '2026-02-04 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'After the Civil War, the Stowes bought a house on the St. Johns River near Mandarin, Florida. For several years, they spent the winters at their Florida home. In 1872, Stowe published Pametto Leaves describing the area, its people and wildlife. The book is organized as a series of articles and includes several ink sketches. It provides a unique view of north Florida and may have influenced Henry Flagler to develop Florida''s east coast as a resort destination.', NULL, 'English', '1873-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5583343-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6300809-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152210W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (300, NULL, 'Betty''s bright idea', '{}', '2026-02-04 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-04 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Betty''s bright idea, by Harriet Beecher Stowe.', NULL, 'English', '1876-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1859867-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1754985-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152216W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (301, NULL, 'Dred', '{}', '2026-02-05 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Harriet Beecher Stowe''s second antislavery novel was written partly in response to the criticisms of Uncle Tom''s Cabin (1852) by both white Southerners and black abolitionists. In Dred (1856), Stowe attempts to explore the issue of slavery from an African American perspective. Through the compelling stories of Nina Gordon, the mistress of a slave plantation, and Dred, a black revolutionary, Stowe brings to life conflicting beliefs about race, the institution of slavery, and the possibilities of violent resistance. Probing the political and spiritual goals that fuel Dred''s rebellion, Stowe creates a figure far different from the acquiescent Christian martyr Uncle Tom. In his introductions to the classic novel, Robert S. Levine outlines the antislavery debates in which Stowe had become deeply involved before and during Dred. Levine shows that in addition to its significance in literary history, the novel remains relevant to present-day discussions of cross-racial perspectives.', NULL, 'English', '1856-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2868502-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/103565-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152165W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (302, NULL, 'Oldtown folks', '{}', '2026-02-05 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Oldtown folks, by Harriet Beecher Stowe.', NULL, 'English', '1869-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5413735-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6090627-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152224W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (303, NULL, 'Key to Uncle Tom''s cabin', '{}', '2026-02-05 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Key to Uncle Tom''s cabin, by Harriet Beecher Stowe.', NULL, 'English', '1850-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6005610-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11314962-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152169W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (304, NULL, 'The Minister''s Wooing', '{}', '2026-02-05 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'From the author of Uncle Tom''s Cabin, a domestic comedy that examines slavery, Protestant theology, and gender differences in early America.First published in 1859, Harriet Beecher Stowe''s third novel is set in eighteenth-century Newport, Rhode Island, a community known for its engagement in both religious piety and the slave trade. Mary Scudder lives in a modest farmhouse with her widowed mother an their boarder, Samuel Hopkins, a famous Calvinist theologian who preaches against slavery. Mary is in love with the passionate James Marvyn, but Mary is devout and James is a skeptic, and Mary''s mother opposes the union. James goes to sea, and when he is reportedly drowned, Mary is persuaded to become engaged to Dr. Hopkins.With colorful characters, including many based on real figures, and a plot that hinges on romance, The Minister''s Wooing combines comedy with regional history to show the convergence of daily life, slavery, and religion in post-Revolutionary New England.', NULL, 'English', '1800-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1471330-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6054522-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152226W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (305, NULL, 'Poganuc people', '{}', '2026-02-05 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Poganuc people, by Harriet Beecher Stowe.', NULL, 'English', '1878-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4457216-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2907087-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL152222W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (306, NULL, 'The Wonderful Wizard of Oz', '{}', '2026-02-05 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Over a century after its initial publication, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz is still captivating the hearts of countless readers. Come adventure with Dorothy and her three friends: the Scarecrow, the Tin Woodman, and the Cowardly Lion, as they follow the Yellow Brick Road to the Emerald City for an audience with the Great Oz, the mightiest Wizard in the land, and the only one that can return Dorothy to her home in Kansas.', NULL, 'English', '1900-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/552443-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12648655-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18417W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (307, NULL, 'The Marvelous Land of Oz', '{}', '2026-02-05 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Tip and his creation, Jack Pumpkin, run away to Oz, where they save the city after it is captured by girls.', NULL, 'English', '1904-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12648656-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/207290-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18396W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (308, NULL, 'Ozma of Oz', '{}', '2026-02-05 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When a storm blows Dorothy to the land of Ev where lunches grow on trees, she meets the Scarecrow, the Tin Woodman, the Cowardly Lion, and Princess Ozma, and together they set out to free the Queen of Ev and her ten children.', NULL, 'English', '1905-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12648657-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4309855-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18415W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (309, NULL, 'Dorothy and the Wizard in Oz', '{}', '2026-02-05 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Dorothy and the Wizard in Oz is the fourth book in Baum''s Oz series. The series chronicles the further adventures of Dorothy both in and out of Oz, as she deals with the characters, situations and desires which continue to spill over from her first fateful adventure.', NULL, 'English', '1908-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12648659-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5927207-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18412W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (310, NULL, 'The Road to Oz', '{}', '2026-02-05 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-05 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Dorothy and her friends follow the enchanted road to Oz and arrive in time for Ozma''s birthday party.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243922-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8431689-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL262390W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (311, NULL, 'The Patchwork Girl of Oz', '{}', '2026-02-06 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, '"Where''s the butter, Unc Nunkie?" asked Ojo.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1473369-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2893454-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18405W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (312, NULL, 'The Scarecrow of Oz', '{}', '2026-02-06 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The adventures of Trot and Cap''n Bill take them to Oz where they help solve the problem of Pom, whose truelove''s heart has been turned to ice by witches.', NULL, 'English', '1910-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/431586-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/765727-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL262352W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (313, NULL, 'The Emerald City of Oz', '{}', '2026-02-06 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'From the book:Perhaps I should admit on the title page that this book is "By L. Frank Baum and his correspondents," for I have used many suggestions conveyed to me in letters from children. Once on a time I really imagined myself "an author of fairy tales," but now I am merely an editor or private secretary for a host of youngsters whose ideas I am requestsed to weave into the thread of my stories. These ideas are often clever. They are also logical and interesting. So I have used them whenever I could find an opportunity, and it is but just that I acknowledge my indebtedness to my little friends.', NULL, 'English', '1910-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1473556-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8923977-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18409W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (314, NULL, 'The Tin Woodman of Oz', '{}', '2026-02-06 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'From the book:The Tin Woodman sat on his glittering tin throne in the handsome tin hall of his splendid tin castle in the Winkie Country of the Land of Oz. Beside him, in a chair of woven straw, sat his best friend, the Scarecrow of Oz. At times they spoke to one another of curious things they had seen and strange adventures they had known since first they two had met and become comrades. But at times they were silent, for these things had been talked over many times between them, and they found themselves contented in merely being together, speaking now and then a brief sentence to prove they were wide awake and attentive. But then, these two quaint persons never slept. Why should they sleep, when they never tired?', NULL, 'English', '1910-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/755973-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2809339-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL262381W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (315, NULL, 'The Lost Princess of Oz', '{}', '2026-02-06 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When Princess Ozma and all the magic of the Land of Oz are mysteriously stolen away, Dorothy and the other residents of Oz are determined to find their missing ruler and the thief responsible for her disappearance.', NULL, 'English', '1912-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/854819-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2893450-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18411W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (316, NULL, 'Tik-Tok of Oz', '{}', '2026-02-06 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'This book introduces Ann Soforth, Queen of Oogaboo, whom Tik-Tok, the clockwork man, assists in conquering the Nome King. Book 8 in L. Frank Baum''s immortal OZ series, in which Betsy Bobbin and Hank the Mule are shipwrecked on the coast of Oz, meet up with the invading army of Queen Ann of Oogaboo, and help the Shaggy Man rescue his brother from the evil Nome King.', NULL, 'English', '1913-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243277-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2893511-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL18414W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (317, NULL, 'Rinkitink in Oz', '{}', '2026-02-06 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When all the inhabitants of Pingaree are kidnapped by the mongrel hordes of twin island kingdoms, Prince Inga and his friend King Rinkitink decide to go to the rescue.', NULL, 'English', '1917-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/765814-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2893519-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL262376W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 4),
    (318, NULL, 'Tarzan of the Apes', '{}', '2026-02-06 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Set amidst the vibrant colors and sounds of the savage African jungle, this classic work, rich in suspense and action, has beckoned generations of readers on a glorious journey to romance and pure adventure. This is the story of the ape-man Tarzan, raised in the wild by the great ape Kala, and how he learns the secrets of the jungle to survive -- how to talk with the animals, swing through the trees, and fight the great predators. As Tarzan grows up he makes many friends: Tantor the elephant, Ska the vulture, and Numa the lion. When this paradise is invaded by white men, Tarzan''s life changes, for in this group is Jane, the first white woman he has ever seen. Speaking directly to our childhood fantasies, this exhilarating work takes us to that faraway place in our minds where dreams prevail, and where we, too, can be masters of our environment. - Back cover.', NULL, 'English', '1912-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6608849-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4636950-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1418251W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (319, NULL, 'The Return of Tarzan', '{}', '2026-02-06 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Return of Tarzan is Edgar Rice Burroughs'' second novel in the series starring the man raised by apes, and the story picks up where Tarzan of the Apes left off. Tarzan finds himself back in the coastal jungle of his upbringing after being thrown off a ship by his deadly enemies.', NULL, 'English', '1914-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8239514-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/747599-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1418249W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (320, NULL, 'The Gods of Mars', '{}', '2026-02-06 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'After the long exile on Earth, John Carter finally returned to his beloved Mars. But beautiful Dejah Thoris, the woman he loved, had vanished. Now he was trapped in the legendary Eden of Mars--an Eden from which none ever escaped alive.', NULL, 'English', '1918-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/207132-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1993510-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1417942W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (321, NULL, 'Warlord of Mars', '{}', '2026-02-06 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Warlord of Mars, by Edgar Rice Burroughs.', NULL, 'English', '1918-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL25547684W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (322, NULL, 'Tarzan and the Ant Men', '{}', '2026-02-06 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-06 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Tarzan and the Ant Men, by Edgar Rice Burroughs.', NULL, 'English', '1921-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10290114-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/762231-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1418079W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (323, NULL, 'The Son of Tarzan', '{}', '2026-02-07 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Paulvitch still lived and sought vengeance against Tarzan. As part of his plot, he lured Tarzan''s young son away from London. But the boy escaped, with the aid of the great ape Akut. They fled to the savage African jungles where Tarzan had been reared. There the civilized boy had to learn to meet the great beasts and face the dangers only his father had ever conquered. But he grew in time into Korak the Killer, almost as mighty as Tarzan. Korak found a friend in Meriem, whom he rescued from a raiding Arab band. Then he discovered that the dangers of the jungle were nothing compared to those devised by men.', NULL, 'English', '1922-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9243231-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8241315-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1418250W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (324, NULL, 'Tarzan at the Earth''s Core', '{}', '2026-02-07 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Continuing the saga of Pellucidar, the empire located in the Earth''s hollow center, Tarzan at the Earth''s Core is the fourth work in this classic series. The American explorer and emperor of Pellucidar, David Innes, has been captured by the deadly Korsar pirates. Picking up on the desperate cries for help emanating from Pellucidar, Jason Gridley of Tarzana brings the message to the only person who can help, Tarzan of the Apes. Together young Gridley and Lord Greystoke travel to the exotic and strange realm within the Earth to save the imprisoned ruler. Unaccustomed to the difficulties of Pellucidar, the two struggle in its savage environment, with its eternal noon and bizarre monsters, in their quest to save Innes and the precarious rule he has established.', NULL, 'English', '1922-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8341280-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/573880-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1418204W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (325, NULL, 'Tarzan and the Golden Lion', '{}', '2026-02-07 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'As Tarzan travels through the jungle to the village of Opar, he encounters a treacherous Spaniard and his party, who intend great harm to the jungle lands.', NULL, 'English', '1923-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8519294-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12386101-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1418088W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (326, NULL, 'Tarzan Triumphant', '{}', '2026-02-07 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Tarzan Triumphant, by Edgar Rice Burroughs.', NULL, 'English', '1932-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11830825-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/15074960-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1418117W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (327, NULL, 'Tarzan and the forbidden city', '{}', '2026-02-07 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Tarzan and the forbidden city, by Edgar Rice Burroughs.', NULL, 'English', '1938-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6615321-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1418193W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 5),
    (328, NULL, 'The Tale of Peter Rabbit', '{}', '2026-02-07 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'One of the best known and loved children''s stories is the story of naughty Peter Rabbit and his misadventures as he is chased around a garden.', NULL, 'English', '1902-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/289591-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/165512-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL108735W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (329, NULL, 'The Tailor of Gloucester', '{}', '2026-02-07 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When the tailor becomes sick and cannot finish the waistcoat for the Mayor, the mice finish it for him.', NULL, 'English', '1903-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/459377-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5814490-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL108770W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (330, NULL, 'The Tale of Mrs. Tiggy-Winkle', '{}', '2026-02-07 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Lucie visits the laundry of Mrs. Tiggy-Winkle, a hedgehog, and finds her lost handerchiefs.', NULL, 'English', '1905-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6567894-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5292119-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL108771W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (331, NULL, 'Tale of Mr. Jeremy Fisher', '{}', '2026-02-07 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A frog fishing from his lily pad boat doesn''t catch any fish, but one catches him - what will happen next?', NULL, 'English', '1906-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7130043-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4989556-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL11553363W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (332, NULL, 'The Tale of Squirrel Nutkin', '{}', '2026-02-07 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-07 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Squirrel Nutkin would rather ask an old owl riddles than gather nuts with the other squirrels', NULL, 'English', '1907-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10028056-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1359565-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL8393099W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (333, NULL, 'The Tale of Tom Kitten', '{}', '2026-02-08 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Tom Kitten and his sisters, Mittens and Moppet, lose their party clothes when they stop to play in a garden. On board pages.', NULL, 'English', '1907-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4574774-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/3344969-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15068176W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (334, NULL, 'The Tale of Jemima Puddle-Duck', '{}', '2026-02-08 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Relates how the barnyard collie and pups rescued Jemima Puddle-Duck from the fox''s cooking pot.', NULL, 'English', '1908-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7347371-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/3078360-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16067296W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (335, NULL, 'The Tale of Benjamin Bunny', '{}', '2026-02-08 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Peter''s mischievous cousin, Benjamin Bunny, persuades him to go back to Mr. McGregor''s garden to retrieve the clothes he lost there.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10447931-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2556200-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL22156524W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (336, NULL, 'The Tale of Ginger & Pickles', '{}', '2026-02-08 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Ginger, a yellow tom-cat, and Pickles, a terrier, run a very popular general store but soon run into trouble because they give everyone unlimited credit.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/459312-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8448428-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL108753W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (337, NULL, 'The Tale of the Flopsy Bunnies', '{}', '2026-02-08 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The six Flopsy Bunnies have a narrow escape from Mr. McGregor''s garden.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5327052-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5327051-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL108698W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (338, NULL, 'The Tale of Johnny Town-Mouse', '{}', '2026-02-08 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'When the country mouse and the town mouse visit each other, they each conclude that there is no place like home', NULL, 'English', '1910-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5328367-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2555973-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL108764W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (339, NULL, 'The Tale of Two Bad Mice', '{}', '2026-02-08 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'While the dolls are away, two curious, naughty mice explore the dolls'' house and steal their furniture.', NULL, 'English', '1917-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6604329-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5327246-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL108768W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 6),
    (340, NULL, 'The Blue Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-08 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A collection of fairy tales from the folklore of France, Germany, Scandinavia, Scotland, and England.', NULL, 'English', '1889-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10323665-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11285708-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088770W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (341, NULL, 'The Red Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-08 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Fairy tales from the folklore of France, Germany, Russia and Scandinavia.', NULL, 'English', '1890-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2839236-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8752451-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088858W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (342, NULL, 'The Green Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-08 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Fairy tales gathered from the folklore of Russia, Germany, Italy, France, China, Scotland, and England.', NULL, 'English', '1892-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2808709-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088797W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (343, NULL, 'The Yellow Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-08 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'First published in 1894, this extensive fairy tale anthology was edited by Andrew Lang, a pioneering author and critic. By bringing together folk tales from all over the world and having them translated into English, many for the first time, he was able to create rich and varied collections of stories, opening readers'' eyes to a whole world of magical possibility overseas.', NULL, 'English', '1894-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5275099-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8582648-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088888W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (344, NULL, 'The Brown Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-08 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-08 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Thirty-two fairy tales from the folklore of Africa, Australia, Brazil, India, New Caledonia, and Persia.', NULL, 'English', '1894-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12025280-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10544147-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088779W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (345, NULL, 'The Pink Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-09 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A collection of more than thirty fairy tales gathered from all over the world.', NULL, 'English', '1897-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10097664-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11083876-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088846W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (346, NULL, 'The Grey Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-09 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A collection of thirty-five fairy tales from the folklore of Lithuania, Africa, Germany, Greece, and France, and other parts of the world.', NULL, 'English', '1900-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2808710-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12371284-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088798W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (347, NULL, 'The Violet Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-09 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'The Violet Fairy Book, by Andrew Lang.', NULL, 'English', '1901-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12014563-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088883W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (348, NULL, 'The Crimson Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-09 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Twenty four fairy tales from the folklore of Hungary, Russia, Rumania, Serbia, Tunis, Finland, Iceland, Japan, and Sicily.', NULL, 'English', '1903-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7113496-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11239898-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088783W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (349, NULL, 'The Orange Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-09 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A collection of fairy tales brought and translated from Rhodesia, Uganda, and Punjaub.', NULL, 'English', '1906-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13463493-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7113667-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088838W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (350, NULL, 'The Olive Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-09 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Twenty-nine tales from the folklore of Turkey, India, Denmark, Armenia, and the Sudan.', NULL, 'English', '1907-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11213284-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088837W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (351, NULL, 'The Lilac Fairy Book', '{}', '2026-02-09 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Thirty-three fairy tales including The one-handed girl and The raspberry worm.', NULL, 'English', '1910-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5709196-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12091706-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1088811W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', 7),
    (352, NULL, 'Cabbages and Kings', '{}', '2026-02-09 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'They will tell you in Anchuria, that President Miraflores, of that volatile republic, died by his own hand in the coast town of Coralio; that he had reached thus far in flight from the inconveniences of an imminent revolution; and that one hundred thousand dollars, government funds, which he carried with him in an American leather valise as a souvenir of his tempestuous administration, was never afterward recovered. Cabbages and Kings was O. Henry''s first collection of short stories, published in 1904.', NULL, 'English', '1904-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8997487-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8997465-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181957W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (353, NULL, 'The Four Million', '{}', '2026-02-09 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'The Four Million is the second published collection of short stories by O. Henry originally released in 1906. There are twenty five stories of various lengths including several of his best known works such as "The Gift of the Magi" and "The Cop and the Anthem". The book\'s title refers to the then population of New York City where many of the stories are set. \nThe stories include;\nTobin\'s Palm The Gift of the Magi A Cosmopolite in a Cafe Between Rounds The Skylight Room A Service of Love The Coming-Out of Maggie Man About Town The Cop and the Anthem An Adjustment of Nature Memoirs of a Yellow Dog The Love-Philtre of Ikey Schoenstein Mammon and the Archer Springtime a la Cart The Green Door From the Cabby\'s Seat An Unfinished Story The Caliph, Cupid and the Clock Sisters of the Golden Circle The Romance of a Busy Broker After Twenty Years Lost on Dress Parade By Courier The Furnished Room The Brief Debut of Tildy', NULL, 'English', '1906-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242997-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6501367-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181960W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (354, NULL, 'Sixes and Sevens', '{}', '2026-02-09 17:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 17:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Sixes and Sevens, by O. Henry.', NULL, 'English', '1911-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8243163-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2037278-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181958W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (355, NULL, 'The gift of the Magi', '{}', '2026-02-09 20:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 20:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Wonderful Christmas story, you laugh and cry at the same time, tender, inspiring, and the best of it is, you know it''s all a storm in a teacup. What they have is priceless.', NULL, 'English', '1906-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/819241-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/683765-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181953W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (356, NULL, 'The Ransom of Red Chief', '{}', '2026-02-09 23:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-09 23:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Two small-time criminals, Bill and Sam, kidnap Johnny, the 10-year-old red-haired son of an important citizen named Ebenezer Dorset, and hold him for ransom. But the moment they arrive at their hideout with the boy, the plan begins to unravel. Calling himself "Red Chief", the boy proceeds to drive his captors to distraction with his unrelenting chatter, malicious pranks, and demands that they play wearying games with him. The criminals write a ransom letter to the boy''s father, lowering the ransom from two thousand dollars to fifteen hundred at Bill''s suggestion. The father, who knows his son well and realizes how intolerable he will be to his captors and how desirous they will soon be to rid themselves of the delinquent child, rejects their demand and offers to take the boy off their hands if they pay him. The men hand over the money and the howling boy – who had actually been happier being away from his stricter father and thus does not want to be "rescued" from his more-lenient captors – and flee after the father threatens to turn his son loose on them.', NULL, 'English', '1918-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5021676-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6796846-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181945W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (357, NULL, 'El Regalo de Los Reyes Magos', '{}', '2026-02-10 02:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-10 02:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'A husband and wife sacrifice treasured possessions in order to buy eath other Christmas presents.', NULL, 'English', '1900-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4909536-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/513394-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181927W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (358, NULL, 'Roads of destiny', '{}', '2026-02-10 05:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-10 05:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'O. Henry''s short, simple stories are noted for their careful plotting, ironic coincidences, and surprise endings. Contents: Roads of Destiny, The Guardian of the Accolade, The Discounters of Money, The Enchanted Profile, "Next to Reading Matter", Art and the Bronco, Phoebe, A Double-dyed Deceiver, The Passing of Black Eagle, A Retrieved Reformation, Cherchez la Femme, Friends in San Rosario, The Fourth in Salvador, The Emancipation of Billy, The Enchanted Kiss, A Departmental Case, The Renaissance at Charleroi, On Behalf of the Management, Whistling Dick''s Christmas Stocking, The Halberdier of the Little Rheinschloss, Two Renegades, The Lonesome Road.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1760023-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2037276-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181949W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (359, NULL, 'The trimmed lamp, and other stories of the four million', '{}', '2026-02-10 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-10 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'O. Henry''s short, simple stories are noted for their careful plotting, ironic coincidences, and surprise endings. Contents: The Trimmed Lamp; A Madison Square Arabian Night; The Rubaiyat of a Scotch Highball; The Pendulum; Two Thanksgiving Day Gentlemen; The Assessor of Success; The Buyer from Cactus City; The Badge of Policeman O''roon; Brickdust Row; The Making of a New Yorker; Vanity and Some Sables; The Social Triangle; The Purple Dress; The Foreign Policy of Company 99; The Lost Blend; A Harlem Tragedy; "The Guilty Party"--An East Side Tragedy; According to Their Lights; A Midsummer Knight''s Dream; The Last Leaf; The Count and the Wedding Guest; The Country of Elusion; The Ferry of Unfulfilment; The Tale of a Tainted Tenner.', NULL, 'English', '1907-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2878076-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2477911-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181941W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (360, NULL, 'Options', '{}', '2026-02-10 11:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-10 11:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Options, by O. Henry.', NULL, 'English', '1909-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1966588-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242951-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181959W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (361, NULL, 'Waifs and Strays', '{}', '2026-02-10 14:00:00.000000+00', '2026-02-10 14:00:00.000000+00', 1, 'Urban teens take center stage in a pair of edgy short story collections. Waifs and Strays presents 15 previously published works by Canadian fantasy writer Charles de Lint, including "May This Be Your Last Sorrow" from The Essential Bordertown and "There''s No Such Thing," which appeared in Yolen and Greenburg''s anthology Vampires. In its first appearance, "Sisters," tells of precocious 16-year-old Appoline, a vampire ("Yeah, I drink blood. But it''s not as gross as it sounds. And it''s not as messy as it is in some of the movies") who plans to wait until her sister, Cassandra, turns 16 before turning her into one, too. Ages 12-up.', NULL, 'English', '1917-01-01', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1279159-L.jpg,https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1758865-L.jpg}', '{https://openlibrary.org/works/OL181946W}', '{}', 'Book', 'book', '{}', '{}', NULL);
